ing, you will be asked to consider and vote upon a proposal to\n138:approve the merger agreement and the merger. At the special meeting, you will also be asked to vote on (1) a proposal to approve, on an advisory (non-binding) basis, the compensation that may be paid or become payable to the Company’s named\n139:executive officers in connection with, or following the completion of, the merger, (2) a proposal to adjourn the special meeting if necessary to permit further solicitation of proxies if there are not sufficient votes at the time of the special\n153:approve the merger agreement and the transactions contemplated thereby, including the merger and the plan of merger. The Board recommends that shareholders vote “FOR” approval of the merger agreement, the non-binding compensation proposal,\n154:and the adjournment proposal.\n163:sign, date and mail your proxy card without indicating how you want to vote, your proxy will be counted as a vote “FOR” approval of the merger agreement and the other proposals. If\n164:you fail to vote, or you do not instruct your broker how to vote any shares held for you in “street name,” it will have the same effect as voting “AGAINST” the proposal to approve the merger agreement but will have no impact on\n165:the outcome of the other proposals.\n208:To consider and vote upon a proposal to approve the Merger Agreement (as amended or modified from time to time, the “merger agreement”) by and among the Company, Genesee & Wyoming Inc.\n210:whereupon the separate corporate existence of Merger Sub will cease and the Company will become a wholly-owned subsidiary of G&W, which we refer to as the “merger proposal”;\n214:To consider and vote upon an advisory (non-binding) proposal to approve the compensation that may be paid or become payable by the Company to our named executive officers in connection with, or following the completion\n215:of, the merger, which we refer to as the “non-binding compensation proposal”;\n219:To consider and vote upon a proposal to approve an adjournment of the special meeting of the Company’s shareholders (the “special meeting”), if necessary, to permit further solicitation of proxies if\n220:there are not sufficient votes at the time of the special meeting to approve the merger agreement, which we refer to as the “adjournment proposal”; and\n238:of directors (the “Board”) recommends that you vote “FOR” the merger proposal, “FOR” the non-binding compensation proposal, and “FOR” the adjournment proposal.\n340:Votes Required to Approve Each Proposal\n381:Proposal to Approve Adjournment of the Special Meeting\n401:PROPOSAL NO. 1—THE MERGER\n409:Background of the Merger\n418:Opinion of the Company’s Financial Advisor\n439:PROPOSAL NO. 2—ADVISORY (NON-BINDING) VOTE ON MERGER-RELATED EXECUTIVE COMPENSATION\n444:PROPOSAL NO. 3—VOTE ON POSSIBLE ADJOURNMENT TO SOLICIT ADDITIONAL PROXIES,\n494:Limitations on Considering Other Acquisition Proposals; Non-Solicitation Provisions\n583:FUTURE SHAREHOLDER PROPOSALS\n599:OPINION OF BMO CAPITAL MARKETS CORP.\n681:proposal to approve the merger agreement, a proposal to approve, on an advisory (non-binding) basis, the compensation that may be paid or become payable by the Company to the named executive officers of the Company in connection with, or following\n682:the completion of, the merger (the “non-binding compensation proposal”) and a proposal to approve an adjournment of the special meeting of the Company’s shareholders (the “special meeting”), if necessary, to permit further\n683:solicitation of proxies if there are not sufficient votes at the time of the special meeting to approve the merger agreement (the “adjournment proposal”).\n688:The Company’s shareholders must vote to approve the merger proposal as a\n689:condition for the merger to occur. If the Company’s shareholders fail to approve the merger proposal by the requisite vote, the merger will not occur.\n714:the merger proposal, “\n716:” the non-binding compensation proposal, and “\n718:” the adjournment proposal.\n730:special meeting, voting as separate classes and not together, is required to approve the non-binding compensation proposal and the adjournment proposal.\n737:will be voted at the special meeting according to the instructions indicated on the proxies or, if no instructions are given, to approve the merger agreement, the non-binding compensation proposal, and the adjournment proposal. If you fail to submit\n738:a proxy or to vote in person at the special meeting, or do not provide your broker, bank or other nominee with instructions, as applicable, your shares of preferred stock or common stock, as applicable, will not be voted on the proposals, which will\n741:” the proposal to approve the merger agreement, but will have no effect on the other proposals.\n818:The proposed merger will occur following approval of the merger proposal described in this document by the shareholders of the Company (with\n860:Opinion of the Company’s Financial Advisor\n882:For more information regarding our financial advisor, see the section of this proxy statement titled “Proposal No. 1—The Merger—Opinion of the Company’s Financial\n912:effective time of the merger (excluding our Chief Executive Officer) will remain in office following the merger until their successors are duly elected or appointed and qualified. Please see the section of this proxy statement titled “Proposal\n984:by the Company, if prior to the approval of the merger agreement and the merger by the Company’s shareholders, the Company executes a definitive agreement with respect to a superior proposal substantially\n995:third party takeover proposal;\n1003:the Board recommends to the shareholders that they approve or accept a superior proposal;\n1007:the Company authorizes, enters into or announces the Company’s intention to enter into a definitive agreement regarding a takeover proposal or a superior proposal;\n1016:business days of being requested to do so by G&W following a publicly announced takeover proposal;\n1039:recommendation) or approves or adopts, recommends to the Company’s shareholders that they approve or adopt, or publicly proposes to recommend, approve or adopt a third party takeover proposal, (ii) failure of the Board to include in this proxy\n1046:recommendation to approve the merger and the merger agreement, (iii) the Board recommending to the Company’s shareholders that they approve or accept a superior proposal, (iv) the\n1047:Company authorizing, entering into or announcing the Company’s intention to enter into a definitive agreement regarding a takeover proposal or a superior proposal, (v) the Company breaching or failing to perform in any material respect its\n1049:G&W following a publicly announced takeover proposal;\n1059:a takeover proposal has been made or communicated to the senior management or the Board or shall have been publicly announced or publicly made known to the Company’s shareholders prior to termination of the merger\n1064:within 12 months of termination of the merger agreement, the Company enters into a definitive agreement with respect to, or consummates, any takeover proposal;\n1068:the Company terminates the merger agreement in connection with entering into a definitive agreement to effect a superior proposal; or\n1080:a takeover proposal with respect to the Company has been made or communicated to the senior management or the Board or shall have been publicly announced or publicly made known to the Company’s shareholders prior\n1085:within 12 months of termination of the merger agreement, the Company enters into a definitive agreement with respect to, or consummates, any takeover proposal; or\n1093:a takeover proposal with respect to the Company has been made or communicated to the senior management or the Board or shall have been publicly announced or publicly made known to the Company’s shareholders prior\n1098:within 12 months of termination of the merger agreement, the Company enters into a d