{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789824180698,"sessionID":"ses_f462b18a6ffeCc3FsyOAV29K5z","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9d5a041001q40232kfZOQgY4","sessionID":"ses_f462b18a6ffeCc3FsyOAV29K5z","messageID":"msg_0b9d597b3001R90NMSFYO4ZR4w","type":"tool","id":"call_00_9ph9ncbzQSbmdPg648H64152","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode/pw && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nblocks = json.load(open('/tmp/opencode/pw/blocks.json'))\n# print blocks from ~150 to ~500 (proxy statement TOC / summary)\nfor b in blocks[186:400]:\n    t = b['text']\n    if len(t) < 200:\n        print(f\"[{b['i']}] p{b['page']} <{b['tag']}> {t}\")\nEOF"},"output":"[186] p3 <p> How to Vote Shares Held by a Broker, Bank or Other Nominee (page 24)\n[188] p3 <p> 3\n[189] p4 <h5> Table of Contents\n[190] p4 <p> Revocation of Proxies (page 25)\n[191] p4 <p> If you have not voted through your broker, bank or other nominee, you may revoke your proxy at any time by taking any of the following actions before your proxy is voted at the special meeting:\n[193] p4 <table> • Timely submitting a new signed proxy card bearing a later date (any earlier proxies will be revoked automatically); or\n[195] p4 <p> If you have instructed a bank, broker or other nominee to vote your shares, you must follow the directions you receive from your bank, broker or other nominee to change your vote.\n[196] p4 <p> Stock Certificates ( page 25)\n[198] p4 <p> Share Ownership of Management (page 26)\n[200] p4 <p> Voting Agreement (page 26)\n[202] p4 <p> Delisting and Deregistration of Our Common Stock (page 43)\n[204] p4 <p> 4\n[205] p5 <h5> Table of Contents\n[206] p5 <p> The Merger\n[207] p5 <p> Structure of the Merger (page 50)\n[210] p5 <p> Closing of the Merger (page 50)\n[212] p5 <p> Merger Consideration (page 50)\n[214] p5 <p> Treatment of Equity and Equity-Based Awards (page 51)\n[215] p5 <p> At the effective time of the merger, subject to all required withholding taxes:\n[218] p5 <p> 5\n[219] p6 <h5> Table of Contents\n[220] p6 <p> Opinion of the Company’s Financial Advisor (page 36)\n[223] p6 <p> Interests of Directors and Executive Officers in the Merger (page 44)\n[227] p6 <table> • the Company’s directors and executive officers are entitled to continued indemnification and insurance coverage under the merger agreement.\n[228] p6 <p> 6\n[229] p7 <h5> Table of Contents\n[231] p7 <p> Conditions to the Merger (page 52)\n[232] p7 <p> The obligations of G&W and the Company to effect the merger are subject to the satisfaction or waiver, at or prior to the closing of the merger, of a number of conditions, including:\n[233] p7 <table> • holders of at least a majority of the outstanding shares of common stock and preferred stock, each voting separately as a class, have approved the merger agreement and the plan of merger;\n[234] p7 <table> • the absence of any order, decree or injunction in effect, or any law, statute or regulation enacted or adopted by any governmental entity, that prevents or prohibits completion of the merger;\n[239] p7 <table> • G&W and the Company must each have performed in all material respects all obligations required to be performed by it; and\n[241] p7 <p> Termination of the Merger Agreement (page 54)\n[242] p7 <p> The merger agreement may be terminated and the merger and the transactions contemplated by the merger agreement abandoned as follows:\n[243] p7 <table> • by mutual written consent of the Company and G&W;\n[245] p7 <p> 7\n[246] p8 <h5> Table of Contents\n[247] p8 <table> • by G&W or the Company, if the required approval of the merger agreement by the Company’s shareholders is not obtained;\n[249] p8 <table> • by G&W, if:\n[251] p8 <table> • the Board fails to include in this proxy statement its recommendation to approve the merger and the merger agreement;\n[252] p8 <table> • the Board recommends to the shareholders that they approve or accept a superior proposal;\n[253] p8 <table> • the Company authorizes, enters into or announces the Company’s intention to enter into a definitive agreement regarding a takeover proposal or a superior proposal;\n[254] p8 <table> • the Company breaches or fails to perform in any material respect its non-solicitation obligations set forth in the merger agreement; or\n[258] p8 <p> Termination Fee (page 55)\n[259] p8 <p> Under the terms of the merger agreement, the Company must pay G&W a termination fee of $3,785,000 if:\n[262] p8 <p> 8\n[263] p9 <h5> Table of Contents\n[268] p9 <table> • within 12 months of termination of the merger agreement, the Company enters into a definitive agreement with respect to, or consummates, any takeover proposal;\n[269] p9 <table> • the Company terminates the merger agreement in connection with entering into a definitive agreement to effect a superior proposal; or\n[270] p9 <table> • G&W or the Company terminates the merger agreement as a result of:\n[271] p9 <table> • the required approval of the merger agreement by the Company’s shareholders not being obtained, but only if:\n[273] p9 <table> • within 12 months of termination of the merger agreement, the Company enters into a definitive agreement with respect to, or consummates, any takeover proposal; or\n[274] p9 <table> • the merger not being completed by December 31, 2016 (or, if the only unsatisfied condition is STB approval of the merger, by February 28, 2017), but only if:\n[276] p9 <table> • within 12 months of termination of the merger agreement, the Company enters into a definitive agreement with respect to, or consummates, any takeover proposal.\n[277] p9 <p> Limitations on Considering Other Acquisition Proposals; Non-Solicitation Provisions and Exceptions (page 56)\n[278] p9 <p> The merger agreement restricts the Company’s ability to solicit or engage in discussions or negotiations with a third party regarding a proposal to acquire a significant interest in the Company.\n[279] p9 <p> 9\n[280] p10 <h5> Table of Contents\n[287] p10 <p> In addition, the Company agreed that neither its Board nor any Board committee will:\n[291] p10 <table> • authorize any of, or resolve, commit or agree to take any of, the foregoing actions,\n[292] p10 <p> 10\n[293] p11 <h5> Table of Contents\n[295] p11 <p> Regulatory Approvals Required for the Merger (page 64)\n[297] p11 <p> Dissenters’ Rights (page 68)\n[300] p11 <p> Market Price of Our Common Stock (page 71)\n[302] p11 <p> 11\n[303] p12 <h5> Table of Contents\n[304] p12 <p> Material Federal Income Tax Consequences (page 74)\n[307] p12 <p> 12\n[308] p13 <h5> Table of Contents\n[309] p13 <p> QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS ABOUT THE MERGER AND THE SPECIAL MEETING\n[311] p13 <table> Q: Why am I receiving this proxy statement?\n[315] p13 <table> Q: What will happen in the merger?\n[316] p13 <table> A: In the proposed merger, Merger Sub will merge with and into the Company, with the Company being the surviving corporation and becoming a wholly-owned subsidiary of G&W.\n[317] p13 <table> Q: What will I receive in the merger?\n[320] p13 <table> Q: What other effects will the merger have on the Company?\n[323] p13 <p> 13\n[324] p14 <h5> Table of Contents\n[326] p14 <table> Q: What are the material federal income tax consequences of the merger to me?\n[329] p14 <table> Q: What are the conditions to completion of the merger?\n[331] p14 <table> Q: When do you expect the merger to be completed?\n[333] p14 <table> Q: When and where is the special meeting?\n[335] p14 <table> Q: What will happen at the special meeting?\n[337] p14 <table> Q: Who can vote at the special meeting?\n[340] p14 <p> 14\n[341] p15 <h5> Table of Contents\n[343] p15 <table> Q: What constitutes a quorum for the special meeting?\n[345] p15 <table> Q: What shareholder approvals are required to complete the merger?\n[347] p15 <table> Q: What shareholder vote is required to approve the other proposals to be voted upon at the special meeting?\n[349] p15 <table> Q: Are there any shareholders already committed to voting in favor of the merger agreement?\n[351] p15 <table> Q: Does the Board recommend voting in favor of the merger agreement?\n[353] p15 <p> 15\n[354] p16 <h5> Table of Contents\n[355] p16 <table> Q: Do any of the Company’s directors or executive officers have interests in the merger that may differ from those of the Company’s shareholders generally?\n[357] p16 <table> Q: Why am I being asked to approve the non-binding compensation proposal?\n[359] p16 <table> Q: What will happen if the shareholders do not approve the non-binding compensation proposal?\n[361] p16 <table> Q: What will happen if the merger is not completed?\n[364] p16 <table> Q: What will happen to my stock options and restricted stock unit awards under the Company’s Equity Plans?\n[367] p16 <table> Q: What if I participate in the Company’s Profit-Sharing Plan or Employee Stock Purchase Plan?\n[370] p16 <p> 16\n[371] p17 <h5> Table of Contents\n[375] p17 <table> Q: How may I vote my shares for the special meeting proposals presented in this proxy statement?\n[377] p17 <table> Q: If my shares are held in “street name” by my broker, bank or other nominee, will my broker, bank or other nominee automatically vote my shares for me?\n[379] p17 <table> Q: What if I fail to return my proxy card or to instruct my broker, bank or other nominee?\n[381] p17 <table> Q: What do I need to do now?\n[383] p17 <p> 17\n[384] p18 <h5> Table of Contents\n[385] p18 <table> Q. What should I do if I receive more than one set of voting materials?\n[387] p18 <table> Q: Can I attend the special meeting and vote my shares in person?\n[389] p18 <table> Q: Can I change my vote after I have submitted a proxy?\n[392] p18 <table> • You may timely submit a new signed proxy card bearing a later date (any earlier proxies will be revoked automatically); or\n[394] p18 <p> If you have instructed a bank, broker or other nominee to vote your shares, you must follow the directions you receive from your bank, broker or other nominee to change your vote.\n[395] p18 <table> Q: What happens if I sell my shares after the record date but before the special meeting?\n[397] p18 <table> Q: Am I entitled to exercise dissenters’ rights instead of receiving the merger consideration for my shares?\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"[186] p3 <p> How to Vote Shares Held by a Broker, Bank or Other Nominee (page 24)\n[188] p3 <p> 3\n[189] p4 <h5> Table of Contents\n[190] p4 <p> Revocation of Proxies (page 25)\n[191] p4 <p> If you have not voted through your broker, bank or other nominee, you may revoke your proxy at any time by taking any of the following actions before your proxy is voted at the special meeting:\n[193] p4 <table> • Timely submitting a new signed proxy card bearing a later date (any earlier proxies will be revoked automatically); or\n[195] p4 <p> If you have instructed a bank, broker or other nominee to vote your shares, you must follow the directions you receive from your bank, broker or other nominee to change your vote.\n[196] p4 <p> Stock Certificates ( page 25)\n[198] p4 <p> Share Ownership of Management (page 26)\n[200] p4 <p> Voting Agreement (page 26)\n[202] p4 <p> Delisting and Deregistration of Our Common Stock (page 43)\n[204] p4 <p> 4\n[205] p5 <h5> Table of Contents\n[206] p5 <p> The Merger\n[207] p5 <p> Structure of the Merger (page 50)\n[210] p5 <p> Closing of the Merger (page 50)\n[212] p5 <p> Merger Consideration (page 50)\n[214] p5 <p> Treatment of Equity and Equity-Based Awards (page 51)\n[215] p5 <p> At the effective time of the merger, subject to all required withholding taxes:\n[218] p5 <p> 5\n[219] p6 <h5> Table of Contents\n[220] p6 <p> Opinion of the Company’s Financial Advisor (page 36)\n[223] p6 <p> Interests of Directors and Executive Officers in the Merger (page 44)\n[227] p6 <table> • the Company’s directors and executive officers are entitled to continued indemnification and insurance coverage under the merger agreement.\n[228] p6 <p> 6\n[229] p7 <h5> Table of Contents\n[231] p7 <p> Conditions to the Merger (page 52)\n[232] p7 <p> The obligations of G&W and the Company to effect the merger are subject to the satisfaction or waiver, at or prior to the closing of the merger, of a number of conditions, including:\n[233] p7 <table> • holders of at least a majority of the outstanding shares of common stock and preferred stock, each voting separately as a class, have approved the merger agreement and the plan of merger;\n[234] p7 <table> • the absence of any order, decree or injunction in effect, or any law, statute or regulation enacted or adopted by any governmental entity, that prevents or prohibits completion of the merger;\n[239] p7 <table> • G&W and the Company must each have performed in all material respects all obligations required to be performed by it; and\n[241] p7 <p> Termination of the Merger Agreement (page 54)\n[242] p7 <p> The merger agreement may be terminated and the merger and the transactions contemplated by the merger agreement abandoned as follows:\n[243] p7 <table> • by mutual written consent of the Company and G&W;\n[245] p7 <p> 7\n[246] p8 <h5> Table of Contents\n[247] p8 <table> • by G&W or the Company, if the required approval of the merger agreement by the Company’s shareholders is not obtained;\n[249] p8 <table> • by G&W, if:\n[251] p8 <table> • the Board fails to include in this proxy statement its recommendation to approve the merger and the merger agreement;\n[252] p8 <table> • the Board recommends to the shareholders that they approve or accept a superior proposal;\n[253] p8 <table> • the Company authorizes, enters into or announces the Company’s intention to enter into a definitive agreement regarding a takeover proposal or a superior proposal;\n[254] p8 <table> • the Company breaches or fails to perform in any material respect its non-solicitation obligations set forth in the merger agreement; or\n[258] p8 <p> Termination Fee (page 55)\n[259] p8 <p> Under the terms of the merger agreement, the Company must pay G&W a termination fee of $3,785,000 if:\n[262] p8 <p> 8\n[263] p9 <h5> Table of Contents\n[268] p9 <table> • within 12 months of termination of the merger agreement, the Company enters into a definitive agreement with respect to, or consummates, any takeover proposal;\n[269] p9 <table> • the Company terminates the merger agreement in connection with entering into a definitive agreement to effect a superior proposal; or\n[270] p9 <table> • G&W or the Company terminates the merger agreement as a result of:\n[271] p9 <table> • the required approval of the merger agreement by the Company’s shareholders not being obtained, but only if:\n[273] p9 <table> • within 12 months of termination of the merger agreement, the Company enters into a definitive agreement with respect to, or consummates, any takeover proposal; or\n[274] p9 <table> • the merger not being completed by December 31, 2016 (or, if the only unsatisfied condition is STB approval of the merger, by February 28, 2017), but only if:\n[276] p9 <table> • within 12 months of termination of the merger agreement, the Company enters into a definitive agreement with respect to, or consummates, any takeover proposal.\n[277] p9 <p> Limitations on Considering Other Acquisition Proposals; Non-Solicitation Provisions and Exceptions (page 56)\n[278] p9 <p> The merger agreement restricts the Company’s ability to solicit or engage in discussions or negotiations with a third party regarding a proposal to acquire a significant interest in the Company.\n[279] p9 <p> 9\n[280] p10 <h5> Table of Contents\n[287] p10 <p> In addition, the Company agreed that neither its Board nor any Board committee will:\n[291] p10 <table> • authorize any of, or resolve, commit or agree to take any of, the foregoing actions,\n[292] p10 <p> 10\n[293] p11 <h5> Table of Contents\n[295] p11 <p> Regulatory Approvals Required for the Merger (page 64)\n[297] p11 <p> Dissenters’ Rights (page 68)