s of common stock outstanding \n[33] p1: Your vote is very important, regardless of the number of shares you own. Whether or not you plan to attend the special meeting, please take the time t\n[34] p1: Table of Contents\n[35] p1: sign, date and mail your proxy card without indicating how you want to vote, your proxy will be counted as a vote “FOR” approval of the merger agreeme\n[36] p1: The accompanying document serves as the proxy statement for the special meeting of our shareholders. This proxy statement describes the special meetin\n[37] p1: Very truly yours,\n[38] p1: Robert H. Eder,\n[39] p1: Chairman of the Board and Chief Executive Officer\n[40] p1: Neither the Securities and Exchange Commission nor any state securities commission has approved or disapproved of the merger or the other transactions\n[41] p1: This proxy statement is dated September 19, 2016 and is first being mailed to shareholders of the Company on or about September 21, 2016.\n[42] p1: Table of Contents\n[43] p1: PROVIDENCE AND WORCESTER RAILROAD COMPANY\n[44] p1: 75 Hammond Street\n[45] p1: Worcester, Massachusetts 01610\n[46] p1: NOTICE OF SPECIAL MEETING OF SHAREHOLDERS\n[47] p1: TO BE HELD ON OCTOBER 26, 2016\n[48] p1: To the Shareholders of Providence and Worcester Railroad Company:\n[49] p1: A special meeting of shareholders of Providence and Worcester Railroad Company (“PWRR,” the “Company,” “we,” “our” or “us”) will be held at Union Stat\n[50] p1: 1. To consider and vote upon a proposal to approve the Merger Agreement (as amended or modified from time to time, the “merger agreement”) by and amon\n[51] p1: 2. To consider and vote upon an advisory (non-binding) proposal to approve the compensation that may be paid or become payable by the Company to our n\n[52] p1: 3. To consider and vote upon a proposal to approve an adjournment of the special meeting of the Company’s shareholders (the “special meeting”), if nec\n[53] p1: 4. To consider and act upon such other matters as may properly come before the special meeting or any adjournment or postponement of that meeting.\n[54] p1: The merger agreement and the proposed merger is more fully described in the attached proxy statement, which you should read carefully and in its entir\n[55] p1: The Company has established September 16, 2016 as the record date for determining the shareholders entitled to notice of and to vote at the special me\n[56] p1: The PWRR board of directors (the “Board”) recommends that you vote “FOR” the merger proposal, “FOR” the non-binding compensation proposal, and “FOR” t\n[57] p1: Under Rhode Island law, holders of preferred stock who do not, among other things, vote in favor of approval of the merger agreement, and who properly\n[58] p1: Table of Contents\n[59] p1: these provisions can be found under the section of the accompanying proxy statement titled “Dissenters’ Rights” beginning on page 68. Under Rhode Isla\n[60] p1: Your vote is very important, regardless of the number of shares you own . All shareholders are cordially invited to attend the special meeting. To ens\n[61] p1: BY ORDER OF THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS\n[62] p1: Charles D. Rennick, Secretary and General Counsel\n[63] p1: September 19, 2016\n[64] p1: YOUR VOTE IS VERY IMPORTANT!\n[65] p1: Whether or not you expect to attend the special meeting in person, the Company urges you to submit your proxy as promptly as possible by completing, s\n[66] p1: Table of Contents\n[67] p1: TABLE OF CONTENTS\n[68] p1: SUMMARY 1 The Parties to the Merger 1 The Special Meeting of the Shareholders 2 The Merger 5 QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS ABOUT THE MERGER AND THE SPECIAL ME\n[69] p1: SUMMARY\n[70] p1: The Parties to the Merger\n[71] p1: The Special Meeting of the Shareholders\n[72] p1: The Merger\n[73] p1: QUESTIONS AND ANSWERS ABOUT THE MERGER AND THE SPECIAL MEETING\n[74] p1: CAUTIONARY STATEMENT REGARDING FORWARD-LOOKING STATEMENTS\n[75] p1: THE PARTIES TO THE MERGER AGREEMENT\n[76] p1: Providence and Worcester Railroad Company\n[77] p1: Genesee & Wyoming Inc.\n[78] p1: Pullman Acquisition Sub Inc.\n[79] p1: THE SPECIAL MEETING OF THE SHAREHOLDERS\n[80] p1: Date, Time and Place of the Special Meeting of Shareholders\n[81] p1: Actions to be Taken at the Special Meeting\n[82] p1: Votes Required to Transact Business at the Special Meeting\n[83] p1: Record Date; Outstanding Shares; Shares Entitled to Vote\n[84] p1: Recommendation of the Board of Directors\n[85] p1: Votes Required to Approve Each Proposal\n[86] p1: How to Vote Shares Held Directly by the Shareholder\n[87] p1: How to Vote Shares Held by a Broker, Bank or Other Nominee\n[88] p1: Broker Non-Votes and Abstentions\n[89] p1: Effect of Broker Non-Votes and Abstentions on Quorum and the Votes Required at the Special Meeting\n[90] p1: How Will Shares Be Voted\n[91] p1: Revocation of Proxies\n[92] p1: Proxy Solicitation\n[93] p1: Dissenters’ Rights\n[94] p1: Stock Certificates\n[95] p1: Proposal to Approve Adjournment of the Special Meeting\n[96] p1: Share Ownership of Management\n[97] p1: Voting Agreement\n[98] p1: Shares Held in the PWRR Profit-Sharing Plan\n[99] p1: Shares Purchased Under the PWRR Employee Stock Purchase Plan\n[100] p1: PROPOSAL NO. 1—THE MERGER\n[101] p1: General\n[102] p1: Background of the Merger\n[103] p1: Recommendation of the Board of Directors and Reasons for the Merger\n[104] p1: Opinion of the Company’s Financial Advisor\n[105] p1: Summary of Financial Analysis of BMO Capital Markets Corp.\n[106] p1: Projected Financial Information\n[107] p1: Delisting and Deregistration of Common Stock Following the Merger\n[108] p1: Interests of Directors and Executive Officers in the Merger\n[109] p1: PROPOSAL NO. 2—ADVISORY (NON-BINDING) VOTE ON MERGER-RELATED EXECUTIVE COMPENSATION ARRANGEMENTS\n[110] p1: PROPOSAL NO. 3—VOTE ON POSSIBLE ADJOURNMENT TO SOLICIT ADDITIONAL PROXIES, IF NECESSARY\n[111] p1: THE MERGER AGREEMENT\n[112] p1: Structure of the Merger\n[113] p1: Closing of the Merger\n[114] p1: Organizational Documents; Board of Directors and Officers of the Company Following the Merger\n[115] p1: Merger Consideration\n[116] p1: (i)\n[117] p1: Table of Contents\n[118] p1: Treatment of Equity and Equity-Based Awards 51 Exchange and Payment Procedures 51 Conditions to the Merger 52 Termination of the Merger Agreement 54 T\n[119] p1: Treatment of Equity and Equity-Based Awards\n[120] p1: Exchange and Payment Procedures\n[121] p1: Conditions to the Merger\n[122] p1: Termination of the Merger Agreement\n[123] p1: Termination Fee\n[124] p1: Limitations on Considering Other Acquisition Proposals; Non-Solicitation Provisions and Exceptions\n[125] p1: The Shareholders Meeting\n[126] p1: Indemnification and Insurance\n[127] p1: Conduct of Business Pending the Merger\n[128] p1: Employee Benefits\n[129] p1: Efforts to Complete the Merger\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Command exited with code 0."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /tmp/opencode/pw && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport json, re\\nblocks = json.load(open('/tmp/opencode/pw/blocks.json'))\\nfor b in blocks[:130]:\\n    t=b['text']\\n    print(f\\\"[{b['i']}] p{b['page']}: {t[:150]}\\\")\\nEOF\"}"},"time":{"start":1789824293473,"end":1789824293777}}}}
