{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825096181,"sessionID":"ses_f462b18a6ffeCc3FsyOAV29K5z","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e39894001ibrPubQ0aoRQ09","sessionID":"ses_f462b18a6ffeCc3FsyOAV29K5z","messageID":"msg_0b9e36d3a001u6pZ2IJNJhxdiN","type":"tool","id":"call_00_QuzH8lu8YEPAGstFRXeE7341","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode/pw && grep -n \"Quotes: \\\"The Company and G&W\\|Quote: \\\"The Company and G&W\\|asked at the Board\\|Asked at the Board\\|source='P-032\\|source='P-030\\|termination fee \\$3,785,000\" build.py | head -20"},"output":"415:    terms='Executed merger agreement (G&W, Pullman Acquisition Sub Inc., the Company): agreed consideration $25.00 cash per common share, without interest; preferred deemed converted 100-for-1 plus accrued and unpaid dividends before the $25.00; no financing condition and G&W representation as to financial wherewithal; termination fee $3,785,000 (approximately 3% of transaction value); outside date 12/31/2016 (02/28/2017 if STB approval is the only unsatisfied condition); non-solicitation with fiduciary out and 3-business-day matching right; no go-shop; G&W to seek STB approval or exemption and to use a voting trust if needed; voting agreement executed with the Eder Trusts (842,742 common; 500 preferred; approximately 17.3% and 78.1%).',\n416:    why='Stated: execution, agreed price, conversion mechanics, no financing condition, termination fee, outside dates, no go-shop; signing records agreed consideration only \\u2014 no bid-price, formality or conditions cells (Convention). Date: Reported day. Quotes: \"The Company and G&W executed the merger agreement, and the Company, G&W and the Eder Trusts executed the voting agreement.\" (P-032, p32); \"the absence of a financing condition in the merger agreement and the representation of G&W in the merger agreement as to its financial wherewithal\" (X-007, p34).',\n417:    source='P-032; X-007; X-013; X-014; X-016; X-017; X-020', wdate=D(2016,8,12), dbasis='Reported day',\n422:    terms='Asked at the Board\\u2019s request whether it would increase its $24.00 offer; declined; the Board then determined the G&W offer was the superior proposal and signed with G&W \\u2014 B was still bidding when the target chose another, so no earlier exit is inferred (Stated).',\n424:    source='P-030; P-031', wdate=D(2016,8,12), dbasis='Reported day', dmethod='Reported',\n432:    source='P-032', wdate=D(2016,8,15), dbasis='Reported day', dmethod='Reported', page=32,\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"415:    terms='Executed merger agreement (G&W, Pullman Acquisition Sub Inc., the Company): agreed consideration $25.00 cash per common share, without interest; preferred deemed converted 100-for-1 plus accrued and unpaid dividends before the $25.00; no financing condition and G&W representation as to financial wherewithal; termination fee $3,785,000 (approximately 3% of transaction value); outside date 12/31/2016 (02/28/2017 if STB approval is the only unsatisfied condition); non-solicitation with fiduciary out and 3-business-day matching right; no go-shop; G&W to seek STB approval or exemption and to use a voting trust if needed; voting agreement executed with the Eder Trusts (842,742 common; 500 preferred; approximately 17.3% and 78.1%).',\n416:    why='Stated: execution, agreed price, conversion mechanics, no financing condition, termination fee, outside dates, no go-shop; signing records agreed consideration only \\u2014 no bid-price, formality or conditions cells (Convention). Date: Reported day. Quotes: \"The Company and G&W executed the merger agreement, and the Company, G&W and the Eder Trusts executed the voting agreement.\" (P-032, p32); \"the absence of a financing condition in the merger agreement and the representation of G&W in the merger agreement as to its financial wherewithal\" (X-007, p34).',\n417:    source='P-032; X-0