{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1789825165221,"sessionID":"ses_f462b18a6ffeCc3FsyOAV29K5z","part":{"id":"prt_0b9e4a7a5001CVoSDrnjZ9vrcq","sessionID":"ses_f462b18a6ffeCc3FsyOAV29K5z","messageID":"msg_0b9e4988400145Ih3Y7B30XwOi","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","cost":0.0012610439999999998,"tokens":{"input":246,"output":239,"reasoning":175,"cache":{"read":325248,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1789825167313,"sessionID":"ses_f462b18a6ffeCc3FsyOAV29K5z","part":{"id":"prt_0b9e4afd1001i6FCbZLo02xoVn","sessionID":"ses_f462b18a6ffeCc3FsyOAV29K5z","messageID":"msg_0b9e4a7b2001mGKFSJ6V1IuDEo","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825169010,"sessionID":"ses_f462b18a6ffeCc3FsyOAV29K5z","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e4b374001GQcBS32jmf81dr","sessionID":"ses_f462b18a6ffeCc3FsyOAV29K5z","messageID":"msg_0b9e4a7b2001mGKFSJ6V1IuDEo","type":"tool","id":"call_00_KTaJox2BO3GM7VwV1MB02438","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode/pw && python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\nwb = load_workbook('/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/providence-worcester.xlsx')\nws = wb['Summary']\nfor r in ws.iter_rows(values_only=True):\n    a = r[0] if r[0] is not None else ''\n    b = r[1] if len(r) > 1 and r[1] is not None else ''\n    if a or b:\n        print('##', str(a)[:110])\n        if b: print('   ', str(b)[:400].replace('\\n',' '))\nEOF"},"output":"## Summary — Providence & Worcester Railroad Company / Genesee & Wyoming Inc. (PWRR-G&W) — AI first pass (not hum\n## STATUS AND COMMERCIAL ACCOUNT\n## Pass status\n    AI first pass; not human-approved. Instruction revision: 19 September 2026 (short form). Supplied source: one filing — DEFM14A for Providence and Worcester Railroad Company / Genesee & Wyoming Inc. (source file raw_filing/providence-worcester_2016-09-20_DEFM14A.htm; proxy statement dated 09/19/2016; background pages 27–32). No other sources used.\n## Commercial account\n    Providence and Worcester Railroad Company (PWRR, NASDAQ: PWX), a regional freight railroad, moved from an unsolicited expression of interest by an unnamed Class I rail partner (Party A) in Q4 2015 to a banker-run sale process. GHF (later BMO) ran one process (rounds 0–3): a 29-buyer outreach wave starting the week of 03/28/2016 produced 25 confidentiality agreements (plus late entrant Party C), ni\n## DEAL FACTS\n## Target\n    Providence and Worcester Railroad Company (Rhode Island; NASDAQ: PWX; regional freight railroad; 4,866,593 common shares and 640 preferred shares outstanding as of the 09/16/2016 record date).\n## Focal acquirer and type\n    Genesee & Wyoming Inc. (Delaware; public; Strategic — operating freight-railroad group owning/leasing 121 railroads; eight North American regions with 114 short-line and regional railroads; operations in Australia and the U.K./Europe).\n## Acquisition vehicle\n    Pullman Acquisition Sub Inc. (Rhode Island; wholly-owned G&W subsidiary formed 08/12/2016 solely for the merger).\n## Agreed consideration\n    $25.00 in cash per common share, without interest, less withholding; each preferred share deemed automatically converted 100-for-1 (plus aggregate accrued/accumulated and unpaid dividends) into common stock before receiving $25.00 per share; all cash.\n## Signing\n    08/12/2016 (merger agreement among the Company, G&W and Merger Sub; voting agreement with the Eder Trusts).\n## Announcement\n    08/15/2016 press release before NASDAQ trading opened (R052).\n## Completion\n    Expected Q4 2016; not observed in this filing (conditions include majority-of-each-class shareholder approval and STB approval or exemption/voting-trust opinion).\n## Filing\n    DEFM14A definitive proxy statement, proxy dated 09/19/2016, first mailed on or about 09/21/2016; filed 09/20/2016 (per supplied filename); source file: raw_filing/providence-worcester_2016-09-20_DEFM14A.htm; background pages 27–32.\n## Labelled calculation — as-converted equity value\n    (4,866,593 common + 640 preferred × 100 conversion) = 4,930,593 shares × $25.00 = $123,264,825 (calculation from disclosed inputs X-004 and X-014; the filing states no total equity value).\n## Labelled note — fee ratio\n    The $3,785,000 termination fee is stated as approximately 3% of the transaction value (X-008); at exactly 3% that implies about $126.2 million on the filing’s fully diluted basis (calculation; no filed total).\n## PROCESS AND ROUND MAP\n## Processes\n    One sale process (Process 1). No abandonment, termination or restart observed; a single winner (G&W) signed.\n## Round 0 (before 03/28/2016)\n    Party A's Q4 2015 approach and interest (R001); GHF engagement 01/27/2016 (R002); Board decision to pursue a change in control strategy 03/14/2016 (R003); Committee authorization 03/24/2016 (R004). Sources: P-001–P-005.\n## Round 1 (week of 03/28/2016; R006)\n    Opening: first outreach wave of 29 contacted buyers (R005). Scope: 25 confidentiality agreements (R007/R008); memorandum; IOI solicitation due 05/10/2016, revised to 05/19/2016 (R011–R013; treatments: Extended, then Enforced); nine IOIs $17.93–$26.50 (R014); two low bidders excluded and seven advanced with management presentations and data-site access (R017/R018); 16 residual non-submitters inferr\n## Round 2 (mid-June 2016; R019)\n    Opening: LOI and mark-up solicitation with due date 07/20/2016 (drafts posted 06/29, 06/30, 07/11). Scope: Party C late entry (R020–R023); six LOIs $19.20–$24.00 (R025–R029, R032–R033); two stated non-submitters (R030/R031). Deadline treatment: Late bids accepted (G&W LOI dated 07/21/2016). Finality: Not final. Sources: P-011–P-014.\n## Round 3 (07/27/2016; R034)\n    Opening: selection of G&W and Party B for confirmatory due diligence and definitive negotiation (R034); four named bidders dropped (R035–R038); D and E re-entered 08/01/2016 (R039–R043) and closed by 08/04/2016 (R044–R047); G&W final bid $25.00 cash 08/12/2016 (R049); signing (R050) and announcement (R052). Finality: Inferred final. Sources: P-022–P-027.\n## Post-signing\n    No competing proposal, go-shop or agreement termination disclosed (through the 09/19/2016 proxy). Regulatory status: G&W filed its STB petition for exemption on 09/01/2016 and submitted a voting-trust form to the STB on 09/14/2016 (X-022) — context only, no ledger rows after signing.\n## Round-bidder tallies (submitting units)\n    R1: 9 (nine IOI submitters, R014). R2: 6 (B, C, D, E, F, G&W; Party C counted on R022). R3: 3 (D, E, G&W; Party B continued without a new priced submission). These are per-round submitting units, not unique firms across the deal.\n## Deadline history\n    IOI 05/10/2016 — Extended (R011/R012; P-009). IOI 05/19/2016 — Enforced (R013; P-010). LOI 07/20/2016 — Late bids accepted (R024; P-014, P-016). No deadline stated for the R1 opening wave or the R3 final stage.\n## PARTICIPANTS AND ADVISERS\n## Named bidders (first activity; last activity; closing outcome and basis):\n## Party A (Strategic)\n    First: Q4 2015 approach (R001). Last: memorandum recipient (P-008). Closed by Inferred: identity row (R016, Count 0) mapping to the 16 non-submitting NDA signers (R015) — see Q3.\n## Party B (Strategic)\n    First: 04/21/2016 introductory meeting (P-007/P-008); first ledger row: $24.00 LOI (R025). Advanced 07/27/2016 (R034). Not selected at signing 08/12/2016 (R051, Stated; Would not improve earlier offer).\n## Party C (Strategic; late entrant)\n    First: early July 2016 approach (R020); NDA (R021); IOI $21.00 (R022) then LOI $19.30 (R028); catch-up access (R023). Dropped 07/27/2016 (R035, Stated).\n## Party D (Financial)\n    First: $21.00 LOI (R027); $24.00 revised LOI 08/01/2016 (R040); paused 08/02/2016 (R044, own statement); closed Inferred: residual 08/04/2016 (R046).\n## Party E (Strategic)\n    First: $21.26 LOI (R026); $23.81 revised LOI with Party F financing 08/01/2016 (R042); withdrew the revision and confirmed $21.26 on 08/02/2016 (R043); closed Inferred: residual 08/04/2016 (R047).\n## Party F (Strategic)\n    First: $19.20 LOI (R029); dropped 07/27/2016 (R038); provided financing support to Party E from 08/01/2016 (R042) after its own exit — no new row or re-entry for F.\n## G&W (Strategic)\n    First: contacted in the opening wave and met at the 2016 Connections Convention 04/03–06 (R005, R010); LOIs $21.15 (R032) and $22.15 (R033); final $25.00 cash bid 08/12/2016 (R049) and signing (R050). Winner — no exit row.\n## Cohorts (not extra parties)\n    11 strategic NDA signers (R007); 14 financial NDA signers (R008); nine IOI submitters (R014); two low bidders excluded (R018); 16 residual non-submitters (R015); one unnamed strategic and one unnamed financial LOI non-submitter (R030/R031).\n## Advisers\n    GHF / BMO Capital Markets Corp. — Company financial adviser (engaged 01/27/2016; BMO succession 08/01/2016; fairness opinion 08/12/2016; fee approximately $2.52 million; affiliate-lender conflict disclosed and reviewed 09/06/2016) — R002. Hinckley, Allen & Snyder LLP — Company legal counsel (first observed 03/24/2016, participating in all Transaction Committee meetings) — P-005. Simpson Thacher & \n## Disclosed attributes\n    PWRR public (NASDAQ: PWX); G&W public (Delaware; non-U.S. operations). Ownership: Eder Trusts 842,742 common (~17.3%) and 500 preferred (~78.1%) — voting agreement; GATX Corporation 4.92% of common; Director Alfred P. Smith (GATX Vice President and Group Executive) recused himself from the bidding-process meetings.\n## COUNTS AND AUCTION SCREEN\n## Contacts\n    Ledger Contact rows: 31 target-initiated contacts (29 in the GHF wave + 2 additional Class I railroads, additive reading; overlap unresolved — Q3). Bidder-initiated first contacts: 2 (Party A Q4 2015; Party C early July 2016), recorded as Bidder interest rows and included explicitly in the contact picture (a Contact tally does not capture them; see formulas below). Filing assertions: “contacted 11\n## Confidentiality agreements\n    Ledger: 11 + 14 + 1 (Party C late entrant) = 26 bidder NDAs; the Board’s Reasons state “25 of whom entered into confidentiality agreements … and six of whom submitted non-binding letters of intent” (X-005) — reconciliation: the 25 are the opening-wave signers; Party C signed later and is the sixth LOI submitter (count difference flagged, Q3). No standstill provisions (P-005).\n## Auction screen\n    MET — more than one independent prospective acquiring bidder unit executed bidder-target confidentiality agreements for this process (25 in the opening wave; 26 including the later late entrant). No lender-only, adviser or rollover-holder agreements are involved.\n## Submissions\n    IOI submitters: 9 (R014) — matches the filing’s “nine written indications of interest.” LOI submitters: 6 (R025–R029, R032–R033; Party C counted on R022) — matches “six LOIs” and “six … submitted non-binding letters of intent.” Stated non-submitters at the LOI stage: 2 (one strategic, one financial — R030/R031).\n## Ledger-derived totals (formulas, Include = Yes only)\n    The Summary cells below use SUMIFS over the ledger columns (What happened = column D, Round = F, Include = P, Count = Q: rows 2–53): contacts; NDAs; bids by round; did-not-submit; dropped; re-entered; reaffirmed; not-selected. Each is a separate event tally and must not be added across steps; blank Count cells (adviser, decision, milestone, access rows) are excluded by construction.\n## Contact rows total (target-initiated)\n    =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$2:$Q$53,'Deal ledger'!$D$2:$D$53,\"Contact\",'Deal ledger'!$P$2:$P$53,\"Yes\")\n## Bidder interest rows total (bidder-initiated first contacts)\n    =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$2:$Q$53,'Deal ledger'!$D$2:$D$53,\"Bidder interest\",'Deal ledger'!$P$2:$P$53,\"Yes\")\n## NDA signed rows total\n    =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$2:$Q$53,'Deal ledger'!$D$2:$D$53,\"NDA signed\",'Deal ledger'!$P$2:$P$53,\"Yes\")\n## Bid rows, Round 1\n    =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$2:$Q$53,'Deal ledger'!$D$2:$D$53,\"Bid\",'Deal ledger'!$F$2:$F$53,1,'Deal ledger'!$P$2:$P$53,\"Yes\")\n## Bid rows, Round 2\n    =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$2:$Q$53,'Deal ledger'!$D$2:$D$53,\"Bid\",'Deal ledger'!$F$2:$F$53,2,'Deal ledger'!$P$2:$P$53,\"Yes\")\n## Bid rows, Round 3\n    =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$2:$Q$53,'Deal ledger'!$D$2:$D$53,\"Bid\",'Deal ledger'!$F$2:$F$53,3,'Deal ledger'!$P$2:$P$53,\"Yes\")\n## Did not submit rows total (16 residual + 1 strategic + 1 financial)\n    =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$2:$Q$53,'Deal ledger'!$D$2:$D$53,\"Did not submit\",'Deal ledger'!$P$2:$P$53,\"Yes\")\n## Dropped by target rows total (2 low bidders + C, D, E, F + D, E inferred)\n    =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$2:$Q$53,'Deal ledger'!$D$2:$D$53,\"Dropped by target\",'Deal ledger'!$P$2:$P$53,\"Yes\")\n## Re-entered rows total (D, E)\n    =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$2:$Q$53,'Deal ledger'!$D$2:$D$53,\"Re-entered\",'Deal ledger'!$P$2:$P$53,\"Yes\")\n## Bid reaffirmed rows total (Party E; Count 0 — its R3 unit is counted on R042)\n    =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$2:$Q$53,'Deal ledger'!$D$2:$D$53,\"Bid reaffirmed\",'Deal ledger'!$P$2:$P$53,\"Yes\")\n## Not selected at signing rows total (Party B)\n    =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$2:$Q$53,'Deal ledger'!$D$2:$D$53,\"Not selected at signing\",'Deal ledger'!$P$2:$P$53,\"Yes\")\n## Per-stage balance (§10.2; units, not spreadsheets rows)\n    R1: 25 entrants (R007 + R008) − 18 exits (16 inferred R015 + 2 stated R018) = 7 continuing. R2: 7 + 1 entrant (R021 Party C) − 6 exits (2 stated R030/R031 + 4 stated R035–R038) = 2 continuing (B, G&W). R3: 2 + 2 re-entries (R039, R041) − 2 exits (inferred R046/R047) = 2 continuing; at signing, Party B closes (R051) = 1 (winner G&W). Inferred share: 18 of 27 exit events (16 residual + D/E at 08/04)\n## Reconciliation notes\n    Outcome tallies are occurrences and affected units, not unique permanent exits (D and E are each closed twice, with a re-entry between). Round-bidder counts are not submissions or unique bidders across the deal. Source totals preserved: 29 wave contacts, 25 wave NDAs, nine IOIs, six LOIs, two LOI non-submitters, two low bidders excluded.\n## COMPARABILITY AND INPUTS\n## Other-scope proposals\n    None observed — all proposals concern acquisition of the whole company’s equity. Party F’s financing support to Party E is not a separate offer or a bidding group.\n## CVR (G&W July bids)\n    $1.13 per share contingent value right, based on the subsequent sale of the Company’s South Quay property; recorded with $20.02 then $21.02 fixed cash at closing; excluded from the final $25.00 all-cash bid on 08/12/2016. Payment timing/formula beyond the sale trigger: not disclosed.\n## LOI comparability\n    LOI prices were “based on different assumptions and requirements related to transaction expenses and change in control payments, which GHF and the Transaction Committee observed could affect the ultimate offer price” (P-021) — not normalized here; treat cross-bidder price comparisons as approximate.\n## Share basis and counts\n    Stated price ranges and implied equity values assume conversion of preferred stock into common stock. Counts: 4,866,593 common and 640 preferred outstanding (09/16/2016 record date and 08/11/2016 measurement date); preferred convertible into 64,000 common shares. As-converted equity value calculation at $25.00 = $123,264,825 (labelled calculation above).\n## Market benchmarks\n    Closing price 08/12/2016 (last trading day before announcement): $16.30 — the Board cites a 53% premium for the $25.00 consideration. Closing price 09/16/2016: $24.88. Q3 2016 trading range (through 09/16/2016): high $25.00, low $15.60 (p71).\n## Glossary\n    NDA — confidentiality agreement. IOI — written non-binding indication of interest. LOI — non-binding letter of intent. Data site/data room — internet data site for legal and financial due diligence. CVR — contingent value right (here tied to the South Quay property sale). STB — Surface Transportation Board; voting trust — arrangement to insulate G&W from unauthorized control pending STB clearance.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Summary — Providence & Worcester Railroad Company / Genesee & Wyoming Inc. (PWRR-G&W) — AI first pass (not hum\n## STATUS AND COMMERCIAL ACCOUNT\n## Pass status\n    AI first pass; not human-approved. Instruction revision: 19 September 2026 (short form). Supplied source: one filing — DEFM14A for Providence and Worcester Railroad Company / Genesee & Wyoming Inc. (source file raw_filing/providence-worcester_2016-09-20_DEFM14A.htm; proxy statement dated 09/19/2016; background pages 27–32). No other sources used.\n## Commercial account\n    Providence and Worcester Railroad Company (PWRR, NASDAQ: PWX), a regional freight railroad, moved from an unsolicited expression of interest by an unnamed Class I rail partner (Party A) in Q4 2015 to a banker-run sale process. GHF (later BMO) ran one process (rounds 0–3): a 29-buyer outreach wave starting the week of 03/28/2016 produced 25 confidentiality agreements (plus late entrant Party C), ni\n## DEAL FACTS\n## Target\n    Providence and Worcester Railroad Company (Rhode Island; NASDAQ: PWX; regional freight railroad; 4,866,593 common shares and 640 preferred shares outstanding as of the 09/16/2016 record date).\n## Focal acquirer and type\n    Genesee & Wyoming Inc. (Delaware; public; Strategic — operating freight-railroad group owning/leasing 121 railroads; eight North American regions with 114 short-line and regional railroads; operations in Australia and the U.K./Europe).\n## Acquisition vehicle\n    Pullman Acquisition Sub Inc. (Rhode Island; wholly-owned G&W subsidiary formed 08/12/2016 solely for the merger).\n## Agreed consideration\n    $25.00 in cash per common share, without interest, less withholding; each preferred share deemed automatically converted 100-for-1 (plus aggregate accrued/accumulated and unpaid dividends) into common stock before receiving $25.00 per share; all cash.\n## Signing\n    08/12/2016 (merger agreement among the Company, G&W and Merger Sub; voting agreement with the Eder Trusts).\n## Announcement\n    08/15/2016 press release before NASDAQ trading opened (R052).\n## Completion\n    Expected Q4 2016; not observed in this filing (conditions include majority-of-each-class shareholder approval and STB approval or exemption/voting-trust opinion).\n## Filing\n    DEFM14A definitive proxy statement, proxy dated 09/19/2016, first mailed on or about 09/21/2016; filed 09/20/2016 (per supplied filename); source file: raw_filing/providence-worcester_2016-09-20_DEFM14A.htm; background pages 27–32.\n## Labelled calculation — as-converted equity value\n    (4,866,593 common + 640 preferred × 100 conversion) = 4,930,593 shares × $25.00 = $123,264,825 (calculation from disclosed inputs X-004 and X-014; the filing states no total equity value).\n## Labelled note — fee ratio\n    The $3,785,000 termination fee is stated as approximately 3% of the transaction value (X-008); at exactly 3% that implies about $126.2 million on the filing’s fully diluted basis (calculation; no filed total).\n## PROCESS AND ROUND MAP\n## Processes\n    One sale process (Process 1). No abandonment, termination or restart observed; a single winner (G&W) signed.\n## Round 0 (before 03/28/2016)\n    Party A's Q4 2015 approach and interest (R001); GHF engagement 01/27/2016 (R002); Board decision to pursue a change in control strategy 03/14/2016 (R003); Committee authorization 03/24/2016 (R004). Sources: P-001–P-005.\n## Round 1 (week of 03/28/2016; R006)\n    Opening: first outreach wave of 29 contacted buyers (R005). Scope: 25 confidentiality agreements (R007/R008); memorandum; IOI solicitation due 05/10/2016, revised to 05/19/2016 (R011–R013; treatments: Extended, then Enforced); nine IOIs $17.93–$26.50 (R014); two low bidders excluded and seven advanced with management presentations and data-site access (R017/R018); 16 residual non-submitters inferr\n## Round 2 (mid-June 2016; R019)\n    Opening: LOI and mark-up solicitation with due date 07/20/2016 (drafts posted 06/29, 06/30, 07/11). Scope: Party C late entry (R020–R023); six LOIs $19.20–$24.00 (R025–R029, R032–R033); two stated non-submitters (R030/R031). Deadline treatment: Late bids accepted (G&W LOI dated 07/21/2016). Finality: Not final. Sources: P-011–P-014.\n## Round 3 (07/27/2016; R034)\n    Opening: selection of G&W and Party B for confirmatory due diligence and definitive negotiation (R034); four named bidders dropped (R035–R038); D and E re-entered 08/01/2016 (R039–R043) and closed by 08/04/2016 (R044–R047); G&W final bid $25.00 cash 08/12/2016 (R049); signing (R050) and announcement (R052). Finality: Inferred final. Sources: P-022–P-027.\n## Post-signing\n    No competing proposal, go-shop or agreement termination disclosed (through the 09/19/2016 proxy). Regulatory status: G&W filed its STB petition for exemption on 09/01/2016 and submitted a voting-trust form to the STB on 09/14/2016 (X-022) — context only, no ledger rows after signing.\n## Round-bidder tallies (submitting units)\n    R1: 9 (nine IOI submitters, R014). R2: 6 (B, C, D, E, F, G&W; Party C counted on R022). R3: 3 (D, E, G&W; Party B continued without a new priced submission). These are per-round submitting units, not unique firms across the deal.\n## Deadline history\n    IOI 05/10/2016 — Extended (R011/R012; P-009). IOI 05/19/2016 — Enforced (R013; P-010). LOI 07/20/2016 — Late bids accepted (R024; P-014, P-016). No deadline stated for the R1 opening wave or the R3 final stage.\n## PARTICIPANTS AND ADVISERS\n## Named bidders (first activity; last activity; closing outcome and basis):\n## Party A (Strategic)\n    First: Q4 2015 approach (R001). Last: memorandum recipient (P-008). Closed by Inferred: identity row (R016, Count 0) mapping to the 16 non-submitting NDA signers (R015) — see Q3.\n## Party B (Strategic)\n    First: 04/21/2016 introductory meeting (P-007/P-008); first ledger row: $24.00 LOI (R025). Advanced 07/27/2016 (R034). Not selected at signing 08/12/2016 (R051, Stated; Would not improve earlier offer).\n## Party C (Strategic; late entrant)\n    First: early July 2016 approach (R020); NDA (R021); IOI $21.00 (R022) then LOI $19.30 (R028); catch-up access (R023). Dropped 07/27/2016 (R035, Stated).\n## Party D (Financial)\n    First: $21.00 LOI (R027); $24.00 revised LOI 08/01/2016 (R040); paused 08/02/2016 (R044, own statement); closed Inferred: residual 08/04/2016 (R046).\n## Party E (Strategic)\n    First: $21.26 LOI (R026); $23.81 revised LOI with Party F financing 08/01/2016 (R042); withdrew the revision and confirmed $21.26 on 08/02/2016 (R043); closed Inferred: residual 08/04/2016 (R047).\n## Party F (Strategic)\n    First: $19.20 LOI (R029); dropped 07/27/2016 (R038); provided financing support to Party E from 08/01/2016 (R042) after its own exit — no new row or re-entry for F.\n## G&W (Strategic)\n    First: contacted in the opening wave and met at the 2016 Connections Convention 04/03–06 (R005, R010); LOIs $21.15 (R032) and $22.15 (R033); final $25.00 cash bid 08/12/2016 (R049) and signing (R050). Winner — no exit row.\n## Cohorts (not extra parties)\n    11 strategic NDA signers (R007); 14 financial NDA signers (R008); nine IOI submitters (R014); two low bidders excluded (R018); 16 residual non-submitters (R015); one unnamed strategic and one unnamed financial LOI non-submitter (R030/R031).\n## Advisers\n    GHF / BMO Capital Markets Corp. — Company financial adviser (engaged 01/27/2016; BMO succession 08/01/2016; fairness opinion 08/12/2016; fee approximately $2.52 million; affiliate-lender conflict disclosed and reviewed 09/06/2016) — R002. Hinckley, Allen & Snyder LLP — Company legal counsel (first observed 03/24/2016, participating in all Transaction Committee meetings) — P-005. Simpson Thacher & \n## Disclosed attributes\n    PWRR public (NASDAQ: PWX); G&W public (Delaware; non-U.S. operations). Ownership: Eder Trusts 842,742 common (~17.3%) and 500 preferred (~78.1%) — voting agreement; GATX Corporation 4.92% of common; Director Alfred P. Smith (GATX Vice President and Group Executive) recused himself from the bidding-process meetings.\n## COUNTS AND AUCTION SCREEN\n## Contacts\n    Ledger Contact rows: 31 target-initiated contacts (29 in the GHF wave + 2 additional Class I railroads, additive reading; overlap unresolved — Q3). Bidder-initiated first contacts: 2 (Party A Q4 2015; Party C early July 2016), recorded as Bidder interest rows and included explicitly in the contact picture (a Contact tally does not capture them; see formulas below). Filing assertions: “contacted 11\n## Confidentiality agreements\n    Ledger: 11 + 14 + 1 (Party C late entrant) = 26 bidder NDAs; the Board’s Reasons state “25 of whom entered into confidentiality agreements … and six of whom submitted non-binding letters of intent” (X-005) — reconciliation: the 25 are the opening-wave signers; Party C signed later and is the sixth LOI submitter (count difference flagged, Q3). No standstill provisions (P-005).\n## Auction screen\n    MET — more than one independent prospective acquiring bidder unit executed bidder-target confidentiality agreements for this process (25 in the opening wave; 26 including the later late entrant). No lender-only, adviser or rollover-holder agreements are involved.\n## Submissions\n    IOI submitters: 9 (R014) — matches the filing’s “nine written indications of interest.” LOI submitters: 6 (R025–R029, R032–R033; Party C counted on R022) — matches “six LOIs” and “six … submitted non-binding letters of intent.” Stated non-submitters at the LOI stage: 2 (one strategic, one financial — R030/R031).\n## Ledger-derived totals (formulas, Include = Yes only)\n    The Summary cells below use SUMIFS over the ledger columns (What happened = column D, Round = F, Include = P, Count = Q: rows 2–53): contacts; NDAs; bids by round; did-not-submit; dropped; re-entered; reaffirmed; not-selected. Each is a separate event tally and must not be added across steps; blank Count cells (adviser, decision, milestone, access rows) are excluded by construction.\n## Contact rows total (target-initiated)\n    =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$2:$Q$53,'Deal ledger'!$D$2:$D$53,\"Contact\",'Deal ledger'!$P$2:$P$53,\"Yes\")\n## Bidder interest rows total (bidder-initiated first contacts)\n    =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$2:$Q$53,'Deal ledger'!$D$2:$D$53,\"Bidder interest\",'Deal ledger'!$P$2:$P$53,\"Yes\")\n## NDA signed rows total\n    =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$2:$Q$53,'Deal ledger'!$D$2:$D$53,\"NDA signed\",'Deal ledger'!$P$2:$P$53,\"Yes\")\n## Bid rows, Round 1\n    =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$2:$Q$53,'Deal ledger'!$D$2:$D$53,\"Bid\",'Deal ledger'!$F$2:$F$53,1,'Deal ledger'!$P$2:$P$53,\"Yes\")\n## Bid rows, Round 2\n    =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$2:$Q$53,'Deal ledger'!$D$2:$D$53,\"Bid\",'Deal ledger'!$F$2:$F$53,2,'Deal ledger'!$P$2:$P$53,\"Yes\")\n## Bid rows, Round 3\n    =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$2:$Q$53,'Deal ledger'!$D$2:$D$53,\"Bid\",'Deal ledger'!$F$2:$F$53,3,'Deal ledger'!$P$2:$P$53,\"Yes\")\n## Did not submit rows total (16 residual + 1 strategic + 1 financial)\n    =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$2:$Q$53,'Deal ledger'!$D$2:$D$53,\"Did not submit\",'Deal ledger'!$P$2:$P$53,\"Yes\")\n## Dropped by target rows total (2 low bidders + C, D, E, F + D, E inferred)\n    =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$2:$Q$53,'Deal ledger'!$D$2:$D$53,\"Dropped by target\",'Deal ledger'!$P$2:$P$53,\"Yes\")\n## Re-entered rows total (D, E)\n    =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$2:$Q$53,'Deal ledger'!$D$2:$D$53,\"Re-entered\",'Deal ledger'!$P$2:$P$53,\"Yes\")\n## Bid reaffirmed rows total (Party E; Count 0 — its R3 unit is counted on R042)\n    =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$2:$Q$53,'Deal ledger'!$D$2:$D$53,\"Bid reaffirmed\",'Deal ledger'!$P$2:$P$53,\"Yes\")\n## Not selected at signing rows total (Party B)\n    =SUMIFS('Deal ledger'!$Q$2:$Q$53,'Deal ledger'!$D$2:$D$53,\"Not selected at signing\",'Deal ledger'!$P$2:$P$53,\"Yes\")\n## Per-stage balance (§10.2; units, not spreadsheets rows)\n    R1: 25 entrants (R007 + R008) − 18 exits (16 inferred R015 + 2 stated R018) = 7 continuing. R2: 7 + 1 entrant (R021 Party C) − 6 exits (2 stated R030/R031 + 4 stated R035–R038) = 2 continuing (B, G&W). R3: 2 + 2 re-entries (R039, R041) − 2 exits (inferred R046/R047) = 2 continuing; at signing, Party B closes (R051) = 1 (winner G&W). Inferred share: 18 of 27 exit events (16 residual + D/E at 08/04)\n## Reconciliation notes\n    Outcome tallies are occurrences and affected units, not unique permanent exits (D and E are each closed twice, with a re-entry between). Round-bidder counts are not submissions or unique bidders across the deal. Source totals preserved: 29 wave contacts, 25 wave NDAs, nine IOIs, six LOIs, two LOI non-submitters, two low bidders excluded.\n## COMPARABILITY AND INPUTS\n## Other-scope proposals\n    None observed — all proposals concern acquisition of the whole company’s equity. Party F’s financing support to Party E is not a separate offer or a bidding group.\n## CVR (G&W July bids)\n    $1.13 per share contingent value right, based on the subsequent sale of the Company’s South Quay property; recorded with $20.02 then $21.02 fixed cash at closing; excluded from the final $25.00 all-cash bid on 08/12/2016. Payment timing/formula beyond the sale trigger: not disclosed.\n## LOI comparability\n    LOI prices were “based on different assumptions and requirements related to transaction expenses and change in control payments, which GHF and the Transaction Committee observed could affect the ultimate offer price” (P-021) — not normalized here; treat cross-bidder price comparisons as approximate.\n## Share basis and counts\n    Stated price ranges and implied equity values assume conversion of preferred stock into common stock. Counts: 4,866,593 common and 640 preferred outstanding (09/16/2016 record date and 08/11/2016 measurement date); preferred convertible into 64,000 common shares. As-converted equity value calculation at $25.00 = $123,264,825 (labelled calculation above).\n## Market benchmarks\n    Closing price 08/12/2016 (last trading day before announcement): $16.30 — the Board cites a 53% premium for the $25.00 consideration. Closing price 09/16/2016: $24.88. Q3 2016 trading range (through 09/16/2016): high $25.00, low $15.60 (p71).\n## Glossary\n    NDA — confidentiality agreement. IOI — written non-binding indication of interest. LOI — non-binding letter of intent. Data site/data room — internet data site for legal and financial due diligence. CVR — contingent value right (here tied to the South Quay property sale). STB — Surface Transportation Board; voting trust — arrangement to insulate G&W from unauthorized control pending STB clearance.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Command exited with code 0."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /tmp/opencode/pw && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\\nwb = load_workbook('/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/providence-worcester.xlsx')\\nws = wb['Summary']\\nfor r in ws.iter_rows(values_only=True):\\n    a = r[0] if r[0] is not None else ''\\n    b = r[1] if len(r) > 1 and r[1] is not None else ''\\n    if a or b:\\n        print('##', str(a)[:110])\\n        if b: print('   ', str(b)[:400].replace('\\\\n',' '))\\nEOF\"}"},"time":{"start":1789825168245,"end":1789825169010}}}}
