{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825189836,"sessionID":"ses_f462b18a6ffeCc3FsyOAV29K5z","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e5013c001t2Z0jz0OPvnSzv","sessionID":"ses_f462b18a6ffeCc3FsyOAV29K5z","messageID":"msg_0b9e4f966001MxSnv6q9UsoPcz","type":"tool","id":"call_00_ET_EZ7b8Yw4UeNnZvey40XE2721","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode/pw && python3 build.py >/dev/null && python3 build2.py && python3 check.py && python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\nwb = load_workbook('/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/providence-worcester.xlsx')\nws = wb['Deal ledger']\nhs = [round(ws.row_dimensions[r].height or 0) for r in range(2, 54)]\nprint('row heights min/max:', min(hs), max(hs))\n# full sample rows\nfor tgt in ('R014','R015','R046','R050'):\n    for r in ws.iter_rows(min_row=2, values_only=True):\n        if r[14] == tgt:\n            print('='*100)\n            print(tgt, '|', r[1], '|', r[2], '|', r[3], '| round', r[5], '| count', r[16])\n            print('TERMS:', r[7])\n            print('WHY:', (r[10] or '')[:1200])\nEOF"},"output":"saved /home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/providence-worcester.xlsx\nsheets: ['Deal ledger', 'Summary', 'Questions', 'Source text', 'Lists']\nheaders OK, 39 columns\ndata rows: 52\nrow ids OK: R001 ... R052\ncounts: {'Contact': 31, 'Bidder interest': 2, 'NDA signed': 26, 'Bid R1': 9, 'Bid R2': 6, 'Bid R3': 3, 'Did not submit': 18, 'Dropped by target': 8, 'Re-entered': 2, 'Bid reaffirmed': 0, 'Not selected at signing': 1}\nbalance after signing: 1 (expect 1)\nsource rows: 55 links checked: 52\nsummary formulas: 11\nformula expected values: [31, 2, 26, 9, 6, 3, 18, 8, 2, 0, 1]\nvalidations on ledger: 15\nquestions: 7\n\nERRORS: 0\nWARNINGS: 0\nrow heights min/max: 40 185\n====================================================================================================\nR014 | 05/19/2016 – 06/01/2016 (received) | Nine IOI submitters (cohort; unnamed) | Bid | round 1 | count 9\nTERMS: Nine written non-binding indications of interest with prices of $17.93–$26.50 per share (assuming conversion of preferred stock into common stock), implying equity values of $90–$134 million; group envelope only, not attributed to members; two lowest later excluded (R018) and seven advanced (R017).\nWHY: Stated: count, price range, equity-value range and share basis. Formality: Informal (Convention) — non-binding indications to a non-binding solicitation; no markups reported at this stage. Conditions: Heavy by context (Convention) — bids made before substantive diligence access (data-room and management access followed the 06/01/2016 advancement). Count 9 = submitting units; price cells hold the group envelope only. Date: due date inside the receipt window (Convention; Assigned: deadline). Quote: \"Between May 19, 2016 and June 1, 2016, the Company received nine written indications of interest (“IOIs”) from potential buyers, with offer prices per share ranging from $17.93 to $26.50 (assuming the conversion of preferred stock into common stock), implying equity values of $90 million to $134 million.\" (P-010, p29)\n====================================================================================================\nR015 | by 05/19/2016 (no submission reported; day of non-submission not disclosed) | 16 NDA signers (cohort; residual; unnamed) | Did not submit | round 1 | count 16\nTERMS: Inferred: residual — 25 NDA signers − 9 IOI submitters = 16 non-submitters; eligible participants were advised to submit by 05/19/2016; the filing identifies the nine submitters and the seven advanced (R017) without these 16; base assumes the 25 wave signers were the eligible population at that date (Party C entered later; the two additional Class I railroads are treated as contacts, not entrants) — see Q3.\nWHY: Inferred: residual — the 25-signer wave (P-005), the nine IOIs (P-010) and the seven continuing buyers (P-010) give 25 − 9 = 16. No decision date, motive or voluntary withdrawal is inferred; only that they did not submit by the due date. Working date = the solicitation due date (Convention; Assigned: deadline). Quotes: \"Each of the potential strategic buyers and 14 potential financial buyers subsequently executed confidentiality agreements.\" (P-005, p28); \"the Transaction Committee concluded that the two low bidders should be excluded from that process. The Transaction Committee authorized representatives of GHF to schedule in-person management presentations with the remaining seven potential buyers\" (P-010, p29).\n====================================================================================================\nR046 | by 08/04/2016 | Party D | Dropped by target | round 3 | count 1\nTERMS: Inferred: residual — the 08/04/2016 decision names the continuing set (G&W and Party B) without D and reports no notice to it; D was out by this transition; the row does not say how or why.\nWHY: Inferred: residual — continuing set named at R045; D’s last appearance is the pause (P-023). Count 1. Decided by Target; Exit reason: Not stated; Working date = the decision day (Convention; Assigned: decision day). Quotes: \"the Transaction Committee directed the management team and representatives of each of BMO and Hinckley Allen to continue diligence and negotiations with both G&W and Party B\" (P-025, p31); \"at which point Party D indicated that it would not proceed with further due diligence at that time\" (P-023, p30).\n====================================================================================================\nR050 | 08/12/2016 | Company and G&W (with the Eder Trusts) | Merger agreement signed | round 3 | count None\nTERMS: Executed merger agreement (G&W, Pullman Acquisition Sub Inc., the Company): agreed consideration $25.00 cash per common share, without interest; preferred deemed converted 100-for-1 plus accrued and unpaid dividends before the $25.00; no financing condition and G&W representation as to financial wherewithal; termination fee $3,785,000