{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825195790,"sessionID":"ses_f462b18a6ffeCc3FsyOAV29K5z","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e51c1d001eIUBDHT8NXe5cg","sessionID":"ses_f462b18a6ffeCc3FsyOAV29K5z","messageID":"msg_0b9e507df001LjwyM01SovLLHe","type":"tool","id":"call_00_7quLlH3GOXVqvlsWnAr30808","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode/pw && python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\nwb = load_workbook('/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/providence-worcester.xlsx')\nws = wb['Questions']\nfor r in ws.iter_rows(min_row=2, values_only=True):\n    print('='*100)\n    for name, v in zip(['Q','Topic','Recommendation','Why/source','Affected','Consequence','Status','Note'], r):\n        print(f'-- {name}: {v}')\nEOF"},"output":"====================================================================================================\n-- Q: Q1\n-- Topic: Process and round map; inferred starts; rejected boundary candidates\n-- Recommendation: Keep one process (no termination or restart observed). R1 opens the week of 03/28/2016 at the first outreach wave (R005/R006); R2 opens mid-June 2016 at the LOI and mark-up solicitation due 07/20/2016 (R019); R3 opens 07/27/2016 on the selection of G&W and Party B for confirmatory and definitive negotiation (R034; Inferred final). Rejected boundaries to retain as their own rows: R003 (03/14/2016 Board decision — outreach began about two weeks later, outside the “about a week” execution test), R004 (03/24/2016 Committee authorization — the alternative anchor under the decision rule), R017 (06/01/2016 advancement to presentations and data site — no updated offers sought; folded into R1), R045 (08/04/2016 prioritization) and R049 (08/12/2016 final bid — inside R3). Post-signing: no go-shop and no competing proposal observed.\n-- Why/source: P-005 (first contact wave); P-010 (advancement); P-011 (LOI instruction); P-022 (selection); P-027 (final bid). Smallest round map that preserves each substantive transition.\n-- Affected: R003, R004, R005, R006, R017, R019, R034, R045, R049\n-- Consequence: Moving the R1 anchor to R003/R004 shifts the round 0/1 boundary and the round assignment of the NDA cohort rows; splitting 06/01/2016 into its own round renumbers R2/R3 and splits the LOI bidders’ round history; treating 08/04/2016 as a new round would move the D/E inferred closes and the G&W final bid.\n-- Status: Pending\n-- Note: None\n====================================================================================================\n-- Q: Q2\n-- Topic: Deadlines, the extension and elapsed-deadline treatments\n-- Recommendation: 05/10/2016 (IOI): Extended — superseded by the 05/19/2016 postponement before arrival (R011/R012). 05/19/2016 (IOI): Enforced — the target moved to selection on 06/01/2016 on the bids in hand; the receipt window (05/19–06/01/2016) straddles the due date but no bid is shown dated after it, so “Late bids accepted” is not supported. 07/20/2016 (LOI): Late bids accepted — G&W’s LOI is dated 07/21/2016 and was considered with no revision of the deadline; the other five LOIs are undated. No deadline stated for the R1 opening wave or the R3 final stage.\n-- Why/source: P-009 (advice and extension, purpose, no requester); P-010 (receipt window and 06/01/2016 selection); P-014/P-016 (six LOIs; G&W dated 07/21/2016). §8.3 tests.\n-- Affected: R011, R012, R013, R024 (also R014, R032)\n-- Consequence: Reclassifying 05/19/2016 as Late bids accepted or Passed without action changes the Summary map and the Working date logic for R015 (16 residual non-submitters) and R014; adding a revision row for 07/20/2016 would imply an extension the filing does not state.\n-- Status: Pending\n-- Note: None\n====================================================================================================\n-- Q: Q3\n-- Topic: NDA/contact populations, count reconciliation and the Party A identity mapping\n-- Recommendation: Record 25 opening-wave signers (11 strategic + 14 financial) plus Party C’s later NDA = 26 total bidder NDAs; the Board’s “25 of whom entered into confidentiality agreements … and six of whom submitted non-binding letters of intent” (X-005) cannot have C inside the 25 and among six submitters; recommended reading: the 25 are the solicited wave and C is the sixth submitter added later. The two additional Class I railroads are recorded as additional contacts (+2), but may overlap the 11 strategic buyers — if so, contacts total 29 and the Class I row becomes a duplicate. The two stated LOI non-submitters (one strategic, one financial) are treated as participants live at the LOI stage; the filing does not identify them or exclude overlap with the excluded low bidders. Party A’s Count-0 identity row maps it to the 16 non-submitting NDA signers (recommended) rather than the nine IOI submitters.\n-- Why/source: P-005 (11 + 14 signers), P-007 (two additional Class I railroads), P-010 (nine IOIs; seven advance), P-013 (Party C), P-014/P-021 (six LOIs; two non-submitters), X-005 (Board count 25/six). Arithmetic: 11 + 14 = 25; 25 + 1 = 26.\n-- Affected: R005, R007, R008, R009, R014, R015, R016, R021, R030, R031\n-- Consequence: If the Class I railroads are inside the 11, the contact total falls to 29 and R009 should be folded; if Party C is inside the 25, the NDA total is 25 and R021 loses its Count 1; changing Party A’s covering cohort changes the identity row’s stated arithmetic but moves no count.\n-- Status: Pending\n-- Note: None\n====================================================================================================\n-- Q: Q4\n-- Topic: Formality and conditions levels; no late-reconfirmation rows\n-- Recommendation: Keep: nine-IOI cohort Informal (non-binding solicitation; no markups at that stage); Party E Informal on the issues-list default, flagged as borderline (a documented response with proposed changes, but no returned agreement markup and no final/binding solicitation); Heavy conditions on G&W 07/21 and 07/26 (three-week exclusive diligence), Party D (four-week/30-day), Party C and Party F (30-day) and Party E (60-day exclusive) — each turns on a stated diligence or exclusivity period; Party B Light (expedited diligence review); G&W’s 08/12/2016 final bid Light (diligence completed 08/11/2016; no financing condition reported, G&W financial-wherewithal representation). No None classifications. No late-reconfirmation row is created: G&W restated its position with a new priced bid on 08/12/2016 (R049), and the target never moved to finalize with Party B on its standing offer — B declined to improve (R051).\n-- Why/source: P-010, P-014–P-020 (LOI terms), P-023 (D/E revisions), P-027 (final bid), X-007 (no financing condition). §9.2–9.3 defaults; late-reconfirmation rule §9.1.\n-- Affected: R014, R022, R025, R026, R027, R028, R029, R032, R033, R040, R042, R043, R049\n-- Consequence: Upgrading Party E to Formal would raise its documentation signal without changing its Heavy conditions; downgrading Party B or G&W would require a reported Heavy trigger; adding a late-reconfirmation row would duplicate an existing priced G&W bid and misstate its Formality origin.\n-- Status: Pending\n-- Note: None\n====================================================================================================\n-- Q: Q5\n-- Topic: Participation outcomes, agency/reasons and every inferred close\n-- Recommendation: Keep the stated outcomes: C, D, E and F dropped 07/27/2016 (Decided by Target; Lower offer than rivals — the Committee cited the finalists’ higher offers); D’s 08/02/2016 Participation paused (Decided by Bidder; Terms or process — it stopped after the Company declined its requested no-signing commitment; a pause is not an exit); E’s 08/02/2016 withdrawal of its revised proposal and price confirmation (Bid reaffirmed; not an exit); Party B Not selected at signing 08/12/2016 (Stated; Target; Would not improve earlier offer); two low bidders dropped 06/01/2016 (Stated). Inferred closes to confirm: 16 residual non-submitters at 05/19/2016 (Inferred: residual; 25 − 9 = 16); Party A Count-0 identity row (Inferred: identity); D and E closed 08/04/2016 (Inferred: residual — the 08/04/2016 continuing set, G&W and Party B, is named without them). Party F’s 08/01/2016 financing support to Party E gets no row of its own because F had already exited on 07/27/2016; it is carried on E’s bid (Support tag) with a Related link to F’s earlier bid.\n-- Why/source: P-010 (exclusions and advancement), P-014 (non-submitters), P-022 (07/27/2016 notice), P-023 (D pause; E revision/confirmation; F support), P-025 (08/04/2016 continuing set), P-030 (B declines to improve). §§10.1–10.2 arithmetic and transition logic.\n-- Affected: R015, R016, R018, R030, R031, R035–R047, R051\n-- Consequence: Treating D’s pause as a withdrawal, or closing D/E at signing rather than 08/04/2016, changes the per-stage balance and the inferred share; giving F a re-entry or group row double-counts its exit; moving Party A’s identity row to another transition changes only its stated arithmetic, not any count.\n-- Status: Pending\n-- Note: None\n====================================================================================================\n-- Q: Q6\n-- Topic: Consideration comparability, the CVR and equity-value inputs\n-- Recommendation: Keep G&W’s July bids with the $1.13 CVR (contingent on the subsequent sale of the South Quay property; fixed cash at closing $20.02, then $21.02) and the final 08/12/2016 bid at $25.00 all cash (CVR excluded). Do not normalize LOI prices for the disclosed differences in transaction-expense and change-in-control-payment assumptions (the Committee and GHF observed they could affect the ultimate offer price). Present the as-converted equity value only as a labelled calculation: (4,866,593 + 64,000) × $25.00 = $123,264,825 (inputs X-004, X-014); note separately that the approximately 3% termination fee implies about $126.2 million on the filing’s fully diluted basis. Market benchmarks: $16.30 (08/12/2016) and $24.88 (09/16/2016); 53% premium per the Board.\n-- Why/source: P-010 (share basis; implied equity values), P-014 (LOI range), P-016 (CVR, cash split), P-021 (expense/change-in-control caveat), X-004 (share counts), X-006 (premium), X-008 (fee ratio), X-012 (prices), X-014 ($25.00).\n-- Affected: R014, R032, R033, R049, R050; Summary deal facts and comparability blocks\n-- Consequence: Adding the CVR to per-share cells would overstate guaranteed cash; converting the disclosed equity values into new per-share prices would invent observations; changing the share base alters only the labelled calculation (the filing states no total equity value).\n-- Status: Pending\n-- Note: None\n====================================================================================================\n-- Q: Q7\n-- Topic: Assigned Working dates and display order within stages\n-- Recommendation: Confirm the conventions used as sort keys (never as observed dates): NDA cohorts at the contact-wave bound 03/28/2016 (R007/R008); Class I railroad contact by 04/07/2016 (R009); IOI deadline set by 04/27/2016 and revision at the 04/28–05/19/2016 midpoint = 05/08/2016 (R011/R012); IOI-stage rows at the 05/19/2016 due date (R013–R016); R2 opening at the mid-June midpoint = 06/15/2016 (R019); Party C approach/NDA midpoints 07/05 and 07/06/2016 and catch-up access bound 07/14/2016 (R020/R021/R023); LOI-stage rows at the 07/20/2016 deadline (R024–R031); 07/27/2016 notices at the decision day (R035–R038); 08/04/2016 inferred closes at the decision day (R046/R047). Equal dates are ordered by # as a deterministic display convention.\n-- Why/source: P-005, P-009, P-011, P-013, P-014, P-022, P-025; §8.1 rules 2–6 and the order constraint.\n-- Affected: R007–R013, R015, R016, R019–R031, R035–R038, R044, R046, R047\n-- Consequence: Changing a convention (for example, using the late-July midpoint instead of the 07/20/2016 deadline) reorders rows within a 