{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825326949,"sessionID":"ses_f462b18a6ffeCc3FsyOAV29K5z","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e71d5c0012Y9nhAcDaQpib1","sessionID":"ses_f462b18a6ffeCc3FsyOAV29K5z","messageID":"msg_0b9e70ad5001JPpOzMuS3yu6Dr","type":"tool","id":"call_00_pn8LWRcMGHBh3VyJhtto5095","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode/pw && python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\nwb = load_workbook('/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/providence-worcester.xlsx')\nws = wb['Deal ledger']\nfor r in ws.iter_rows(min_row=2, values_only=True):\n    print(f\"[{r[14]}] {r[3]}: {r[7]}\")\n    print()\nEOF"},"output":"[R001] Bidder interest: Party A suggested possible joint venture arrangements and expressed interest in acquiring equity in the Company during a meeting with Chairman/CEO Eder and VP Rogers called to discuss joint commercial opportunities; bidder-initiated first contact; no price discussed. Led to the Board’s banker search (R002).\n\n[R002] Adviser engaged: Retained GHF (Greene Holcomb & Fisher LLC) as investment banking firm after a subcommittee of two independent directors (Barrett, Anderson) interviewed several firms; subcommittee recommended retention and the Board approved on 01/27/2016; GHF represented it would not represent any potential buyer of the Company or any person proposing financing; GHF’s business acquired by BMO Capital Markets Corp. on 08/01/2016 (successor — one adviser relationship); rendered the 08/12/2016 fairness opinion (oral, confirmed in writing); fee approximately $2.52 million; on 09/06/2016 the Board reviewed BMO’s disclosure that a BMO affiliate holds an approximately 5% participation in G&W’s senior secured syndicated facility and confirmed it was not material to BMO’s independence.\n\n[R003] Target sale decision: Special Board meeting: GHF presented its evaluation of the business and industry and proposed a process — discussions with Party A plus solicitation of other potential third parties for a change in control transaction; Board concluded it was in the Company’s best interest to proceed and appointed the Transaction Committee (Barrett (Chair), Anderson, Garvey) to supervise the process and recommend to the full Board; the Committee could not approve or enter a change of control transaction (full-Board authority under Rhode Island law). Candidate R1 anchor (rejected — R007).\n\n[R004] Target decision: Following management’s 03/22–23/2016 meetings with Party A (Party A informed of GHF’s engagement), the Committee authorized GHF to contact Party A and other potential buyers to determine their interest in a change in control transaction. Candidate R1 anchor (rejected — outreach wave preferred; R007).\n\n[R005] Contact: Outreach wave (strategic): GHF contacted 11 potential strategic buyers (including Party A) to determine their interest in a change in control transaction; the 18 financial buyers contacted in the same wave are recorded at R006; two additional Class I railroads approached by management are recorded separately (R010); five strategic buyers (including G&W) had introductory meetings at the 2016 Connections Convention 04/03–04/06 (folded into R011).\n\n[R006] Contact: Outreach wave (financial): GHF contacted 18 potential financial buyers to determine their interest in a change in control transaction; 14 of them later executed confidentiality agreements (R009); the strategic cohort is R005.\n\n[R007] Round opened: R1 anchor: first outreach wave (week of 03/28/2016; R005/R006) — other candidate anchors: R003 (03/14/2016 Board decision to proceed; outreach began about two weeks later) and R004 (03/24/2016 Committee authorization; outreach began the following week); rejected because the first outreach wave takes precedence. Round finality: Not final — the IOI solicitation was non-binding and no final or binding stage was announced.\n\n[R008] NDA signed: All 11 contacted potential strategic buyers executed confidentiality agreements; agreements contained no standstill or similar provision; signers later received the Company memorandum and, when advanced, internet data-site access (R018). G&W, Party A and Party B are covered by this cohort (no separate NDA rows).\n\n[R009] NDA signed: 14 of the 18 contacted potential financial buyers executed confidentiality agreements (four did not); agreements contained no standstill or similar provision; signers received the memorandum and, when advanced, data-site access.\n\n[R010] Contact: Management also approached two additional Class I railroads to determine their interest in a possible transaction; treated as additive to the 29 GHF contacts (reading \"additional\"); possible overlap with the 11 contacted strategic buyers is unresolved (Q3).\n\n[R011] Target decision: Committee discussed the process to date; authorized GHF to contact the five interested parties met at the 2016 Connections Convention (including G&W) plus other potential strategic buyers and NDA-holding private equity firms to confirm continuing interest; Party B’s introductory meeting followed on 04/21/2016.\n\n[R012] Deadline set: IOI due date: each potential buyer was advised to submit a non-binding indication of interest by 05/10/2016; superseded by the 05/19/2016 postponement (R013). Due date 05/10/2016; treatment Extended (moved by a revision before arrival).\n\n[R013] Deadline revised: IOI deadline postponed from 05/10/2016 to 05/19/2016 \"to ensure the potential buyers had sufficient time to formulate their most compelling offers\"; requester not disclosed; new due date 05/19/2016 (treatment Enforced).\n\n[R014] Deadline: Scheduled IOI due date reached while operative; the target then considered the nine IOIs received 05/19–06/01/2016 and moved to selection (06/01/2016) on the bids in hand — no extension; treatment Enforced (no bid shown dated after the due date: the receipt window straddles it; Q2).\n\n[R015] Bid: Nine written non-binding indications of interest with prices of $17.93–$26.50 per share (assuming conversion of preferred stock into common stock), implying equity values of $90–$134 million; group envelope only, not attributed to members; two lowest later excluded (R019) and seven advanced (R018).\n\n[R016] Did not submit: Inferred: residual — 25 NDA signers − 9 IOI submitters = 16 non-submitters; eligible participants were advised to submit by 05/19/2016; the filing identifies the nine submitters and the seven advanced (R018) without these 16; base assumes the 25 wave signers were the eligible population at that date (Party C entered later; the two additional Class I railroads are treated as contacts, not entrants) — see Q3.\n\n[R017] Did not submit: Inferred: identity — Party A appears individually only through the opening wave and the memorandum distribution (P-008) and is never mentioned again; recommended reading: already counted within the 16 non-submitting NDA signers (R016, Did not submit 05/19/2016); alternative: within the nine IOI submitters (R015). No count is moved from the cohort (Count 0); see Q3.\n\n[R018] Target decision: Committee considered the nine IOIs; excluded the two low bidders (R019) and authorized in-person management presentations for the remaining seven, permitting additional due diligence with access to an internet data site (access alike for the advancing set); over June–July each advancing buyer and its advisers conducted diligence, including management meetings.\n\n[R019] Dropped by target: Excluded from the management-presentation process as the two lowest IOI bidders; identities and prices not disclosed (within the R015 envelope); denied the management-presentation and data-room stage.\n\n[R020] Round opened: R2 opens: Committee-directed instruction to all potential buyers to submit non-binding LOIs by 07/20/2016 together with mark-ups of the merger agreement, disclosure letter and voting agreement (initial drafts posted to the data site 06/29, 06/30 and 07/11/2016); buyers to value 100% of the outstanding common stock on a per-share basis (assuming preferred conversion) or give non-cash terms. Round finality: Not final (non-binding LOI stage).\n\n[R021] Bidder interest: Party C approached Company management and expressed interest in acquiring the Company; not previously part of the process; bidder-initiated first contact; led to an NDA and catch-up access (R022, R024) and an IOI (R023).\n\n[R022] NDA signed: Executed a confidentiality agreement, then was provided the memorandum given to the other potential buyers; late entrant tracked separately from the 25 opening-wave signers (Q3).\n\n[R023] Bid: IOI to acquire the Company at $21.00 per share (implying an equity value of $108 million); later revised in its LOI (R029); count 1 = Party C’s first R2 submission.\n\n[R024] Information access changed: Late-entrant catch-up access: after its IOI, Party C was provided access to the internet data site used by the other advancing buyers and a telephone management presentation on 07/14/2016; access compressed into the LOI window relative to the others’ June–July access; Count blank (access decision).\n\n[R025] Deadline: Scheduled LOI due date reached; six LOIs received in late July 2016 and considered; one (G&W) dated 07/21/2016 after the due date, with no revision of the deadline — treatment: Late bids accepted.\n\n[R026] Bid: LOI to acquire the Company at $24.00 per share, subject to an expedited diligence review; provided mark-ups of the merger agreement and voting agreement; highest-priced offer at the LOI stage; advanced to confirmatory diligence with G&W (R035).\n\n[R027] Bid: LOI at $21.26 per share, subject to a 60-day exclusivity period for due diligence and negotiation of definitive documentation; provided a summary of material issues and proposed changes to the merger agreement and voting agreement (an issues list, not a returned markup — borderline formality, Q4).\n\n[R028] Bid: LOI at $21.00 per share, subject to a four-week diligence period; provided mark-ups of the merger agreement and voting agreement.\n\n[R029] Bid: LOI at $19.30 per share, subject to a 30-day diligence period; lower than its $21.00 IOI (R023); no markup or formal signal reported. Count 0 — Party C’s R2 bidder count is carried on R023.\n\n[R030] Bid: LOI at $19.20 per share, subject to a 30-day due diligence period; no markup or other formal signal reported.\n\n[R031] Did not submit: Elected not to submit an LOI in the 07/20/2016 solicitation while in the process at that stage; identity not disclosed; may overlap other unnamed cohorts (Q3).\n\n[R032] Did not submit: Elected not to submit an LOI in the 07/20/2016 solicitation while in the process at that stage; identity not disclosed; may overlap other unnamed cohorts (Q3).\n\n[R033] Bid: LOI at $21.15 per share = $20.02 cash at closing + $1.13 CVR (contingent value right based on the subsequent sale of the South Quay property); subject to a three-week exclusive diligence period; provided a markup of the disclosure letter and (with its LOIs) mark-ups of the merger agreement and voting agreement; revised 07/26/2016 (R034).\n\n[R034] Bid: Revised LOI at $22.15 per share = $21.02 cash at closing + $1.13 CVR (unchanged), after GHF feedback that the price and CVR structure were not competitive. Count 0 — second R2 submission by G&W; R033 carries its R2 bidder count.\n\n[R035] Round opened: R3 opens: the Committee concluded to proceed with confirmatory due diligence and negotiations with G&W and Party B because of their higher offers relative to the other potential buyers; remaining bidders informed they were no longer involved (R036–R038); on-site financial, legal and environmental diligence and hi-rail inspections by both finalists 07/27–08/11/2016 (access alike for the advancing set). Round finality: Inferred final (moved to definitive negotiation with selected bidders).\n\n[R036] Dropped by target: Told no longer involved after the decision to proceed with G&W and Party B; offered $19.30 at the LOI stage versus the finalists’ $24.00 and $22.15; denied the confirmatory and definitive stage (R3).\n\n[R037] Dropped by target: Told no longer involved after the decision to proceed with G&W and Party B; offered $21.00 at the LOI stage versus the finalists’ $24.00 and $22.15; denied the confirmatory and definitive stage (R3).\n\n[R038] Dropped by target: Told no longer involved after the decision to proceed with G&W and Party B; offered $21.26 at the LOI stage versus the finalists’ $24.00 and $22.15; denied the confirmatory and definitive stage (R3).\n\n[R039] Dropped by target: Told no longer involved after the decision to proceed with G&W and Party B; offered $19.20 at the LOI stage versus the finalists’ $24.00 and $22.15; denied the confirmatory and definitive stage (R3).\n\n[R040] Re-entered: Renewed participation after its 07/27/2016 exclusion: D and E expressed interest in re-engaging on GHF’s 07/29/2016 calls and D submitted a revised LOI on 08/01/2016 (R041) — actual renewed activity, not a mere request.\n\n[R041] Bid: Revised LOI at $24.00 per share (up from $21.00, R028), subject to a 30-day due diligence period; D asked the Company not to enter an agreement with another bidder during that period; the Company declined; D then indicated it would not proceed with further diligence at that time (R045).\n\n[R042] Re-entered: Renewed participation after its 07/27/2016 exclusion: E expressed interest in re-engaging on GHF’s 07/29/2016 calls and submitted a revised LOI on 08/01/2016 (R043) — actual renewed activity, not a mere request.\n\n[R043] Bid: Support: Party F (financing) — revised LOI at $23.81 per share with financing support from Party F, subject to a 30-day due diligence period; F’s independent participation had ended on 07/27/2016 (R039), so F gets no new row and no re-entry; F’s earlier bid: R030.\n\n[R044] Bid reaffirmed: Reaffirmed by: price confirmed — withdrew its revised $23.81 proposal and confirmed its original proposal of $21.26 per share; the original terms (60-day exclusive diligence and negotiation period) carried forward; the revised proposal stands withdrawn.\n\n[R045] Participation paused: D declined to shorten its 30-day diligence period and asked the Company not to sign with another bidder during it; the Company declined; D indicated it would not proceed with further due diligence \"at that time\" — D’s own stated temporary stop, not a withdrawal; D remains live (closed at R047).\n\n[R046] Target decision: Committee directed continued diligence and negotiations with both G&W and Party B, but to prioritize Party B and complete the merger agreement with it, given Party B’s higher price; D and E are not in the continuing set (closes R047, R048).\n\n[R047] Dropped by target: Inferred: residual — the 08/04/2016 decision names the continuing set (G&W and Party B) without D and reports no notice to it; D was out by this transition; the row does not say how or why.\n\n[R048] Dropped by target: Inferred: residual — the 08/04/2016 decision names the continuing set (G&W and Party B) without E and reports no notice to it; E was out by this transition; the row does not say how or why.\n\n[R049] Target decision: Directed BMO to inform G&W that the Company intended to enter into a merger agreement with another bidder (Party B); G&W requested and was granted continued due diligence, including physical diligence on 08/10–08/11/2016, to potentially facilitate an improved offer.\n\n[R050] Bid: Revised LOI at $25.00 per share in cash, excluding the previously proposed CVR, with mark-ups of the merger agreement and voting agreement; submitted the morning of 08/12/2016 after G&W completed physical diligence (08/11/2016) and after its 08/11/2016 indication of a possible revised LOI; offer stated to expire at 6:00 p.m. on 08/13/2016.\n\n[R051] Merger agreement signed: Executed merger agreement (G&W, Pullman Acquisition Sub Inc., the Company): agreed consideration $25.00 cash per common share, without interest; preferred deemed converted 100-for-1 plus accrued and unpaid dividends before the $25.00; no financing condition and G&W representation as to financial wherewithal; termination fee $3,785,000 (approximately 3% of transaction value; negotiated down from 3.85% and lower than Party B’s fee of 3% plus capped transaction expenses); outside date 12/31/2016 (02/28/2017 if STB approval is the only unsatisfied condition); non-solicitation with fiduciary out and 3-business-day matching right; no go-shop; G&W to seek STB approval or exemption and to use a voting trust if needed; voting agreement executed with the Eder Trusts (842,742 common; 500 preferred; approximately 17.3% and 78.1%).\n\n[R052] Not selected at signing: Asked at the Board’s request (after the Committee directed that it be told a higher revised LOI had been received) whether it would increase its $24.00 offer; declined; the Board then determined the G&W offer was the superior proposal and signed with G&W — B was still bidding when the target chose another, so no earlier exit is inferred (Stated).\n\n[R053] Merger announced: PWRR issued a press release publicly announcing the transaction before the opening of NASDAQ trading on Monday 08/15/2016.\n\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"[R001] Bidder interest: Party A suggested possible joint venture arrangements and expressed interest in acquiring equity in the Company during a meeting with Chairman/CEO Eder and VP Rogers called to discuss joint commercial opportunities; bidder-initiated first contact; no price discussed. Led to the Board’s banker search (R002).\n\n[R002] Adviser engaged: Retained GHF (Greene Holcomb & Fisher LLC) as investment banking firm after a subcommittee of two independent directors (Barrett, Anderson) interviewed several firms; subcommittee recommended retention and the Board approved on 01/27/2016; GHF represented it would not represent any potential buyer of the Company or any person proposing financing; GHF’s business acquired by BMO Capital Markets Corp. on 08/01/2016 (successor — one adviser relationship); rendered the 08/12/2016 fairness opinion (oral, confirmed in writing); fee approximately $2.52 million; on 09/06/2016 the Board reviewed BMO’s disclosure that a BMO affiliate holds an approximately 5% participation in G&W’s senior secured syndicated facility and confirmed it was not material to BMO’s independence.\n\n[R003] Target sale decision: Special Board meeting: GHF presented its evaluation of the business and industry and proposed a process — discussions with Party A plus solicitation of other potential third parties for a change in control transaction; Board concluded it was in the Company’s best interest to proceed and appointed the Transaction Committee (Barrett (Chair), Anderson, Garvey) to supervise the process and recommend to the full Board; the Committee could not approve or enter a change of control transaction (full-Board authority under Rhode Island law). Candidate R1 anchor (rejected — R007).\n\n[R004] Target decision: Following management’s 03/22–23/2016 meetings with Party A (Party A informed of GHF’s engagement), the Committee authorized GHF to contact Party A and other potential buyers to determine their interest in a change in control transaction. Candidate R1 anchor (rejected — outreach wave preferred; R007).\n\n[R005] Contact: Outreach wave (strategic): GHF contacted 11 potential strategic buyers (including Party A) to determine their interest in a change in control transaction; the 18 financial buyers contacted in the same wave are recorded at R006; two additional Class I railroads approached by management are recorded separately (R010); five strategic buyers (including G&W) had introductory meetings at the 2016 Connections Convention 04/03–04/06 (folded into R011).\n\n[R006] Contact: Outreach wave (financial): GHF contacted 18 potential financial buyers to determine their interest in a change in control transaction; 14 of them later executed confidentiality agreements (R009); the strategic cohort is R005.\n\n[R007] Round opened: R1 anchor: first outreach wave (week of 03/28/2016; R005/R006) — other candidate anchors: R003 (03/14/2016 Board decision to proceed; outreach began about two weeks later) and R004 (03/24/2016 Committee authorization; outreach began the following week); rejected because the first outreach wave takes precedence. Round finality: Not final — the IOI solicitation was non-binding and no final or binding stage was announced.\n\n[R008] NDA signed: All 11 contacted potential strategic buyers executed confidentiality agreements; agreements contained no standstill or similar provision; signers later received the Company memorandum and, when advanced, internet data-site access (R018). G&W, Party A and Party B are covered by this cohort (no separate NDA rows).\n\n[R009] NDA signed: 14 of the 18 contacted potential financial buyers executed confidentiality agreements (four did not); agreements contained no standstill or similar provision; signers received the memorandum and, when advanced, data-site access.\n\n[R010] Contact: Management also approached two additional Class I railroads to determine their interest in a possible transaction; treated as additive to the 29 GHF contacts (reading \"additional\"); possible overlap with the 11 contacted strategic buyers is unresolved (Q3).\n\n[R011] Target decision: Committee discussed the process to date; authorized GHF to contact the five interested parties met at the 2016 Connections Convention (including G&W) plus other potential strategic buyers and NDA-holding private equity firms to confirm continuing interest; Party B’s introductory meeting followed on 04/21/2016.\n\n[R012] Deadline set: IOI due date: each potential buyer was advised to submit a non-binding indication of interest by 05/10/2016; superseded by the 05/19/2016 postponement (R013). Due date 05/10/2016; treatment Extended (moved by a revision before arrival).\n\n[R013] Deadline revised: IOI deadline postponed from 05/10/2016 to 05/19/2016 \"to ensure the potential buyers had sufficient time to formulate their most compelling offers\"; requester not disclosed; new due date 05/19/2016 (treatment Enforced).\n\n[R014] Deadline: Scheduled IOI due date reached while operative; the target then considered the nine IOIs received 05/19–06/01/2016 and moved to selection (06/01/2016) on the bids in hand — no extension; treatment Enforced (no bid shown dated after the due date: the receipt window straddles it; Q2).\n\n[R015] Bid: Nine written non-binding indications of interest with prices of $17.93–$26.50 per share (assuming conversion of preferred stock into common stock), implying equity values of $90–$134 million; group envelope only, not attributed to members; two lowest later excluded (R019) and seven advanced (R018).\n\n[R016] Did not submit: Inferred: residual — 25 NDA signers − 9 IOI submitters = 16 non-submitters; eligible participants were advised to submit by 05/19/2016; the filing identifies the nine submitters and the seven advanced (R018) without these 16; base assumes the 25 wave signers were the eligible population at that date (Party C entered later; the two additional Class I railroads are treated as contacts, not entrants) — see Q3.\n\n[R017] Did not submit: Inferred: identity — Party A appears individually only through the opening wave and the memorandum distribution (P-008) and is never mentioned again; recommended reading: already counted within the 16 non-submitting NDA signers (R016, Did not submit 05/19/2016); alternative: within the nine IOI submitters (R015). No count is moved from the cohort (Count 0); see Q3.\n\n[R018] Target decision: Committee considered the nine IOIs; excluded the two low bidders (R019) and authorized in-person management presentations for the remaining seven, permitting additional due diligence with access to an internet data site (access alike for the advancing set); over June–July each advancing buyer and its advisers conducted diligence, including management meetings.\n\n[R019] Dropped by target: Excluded from the management-presentation process as the two lowest IOI bidders; identities and prices not disclosed (within the R015 envelope); denied the management-presentation and data-room stage.\n\n[R020] Round opened: R2 opens: Committee-directed instruction to all potential buyers to submit non-binding LOIs by 07/20/2016 together with mark-ups of the merger agreement, disclosure letter and voting agreement (initial drafts posted to the data site 06/29, 06/30 and 07/11/2016); buyers to value 100% of the outstanding common stock on a per-share basis (assuming preferred conversion) or give non-cash terms. Round finality: Not final (non-binding LOI stage).\n\n[R021] Bidder interest: Party C approached Company management and expressed interest in acquiring the Company; not previously part of the process; bidder-initiated first contact; led to an NDA and catch-up access (R022, R024) and an IOI (R023).\n\n[R022] NDA signed: Executed a confidentiality agreement, then was provided the memorandum given to the other potential buyers; late entrant tracked separately from the 25 opening-wave signers (Q3).\n\n[R023] Bid: IOI to acquire the Company at $21.00 per share (implying an equity value of $108 million); later revised in its LOI (R029); count 1 = Party C’s first R2 submission.\n\n[R024] Information access changed: Late-entrant catch-up access: after its IOI, Party C was provided access to the internet data site used by the other advancing buyers and a telephone management presentation on 07/14/2016; access compressed into the LOI window relative to the others’ June–July access; Count blank (access decision).\n\n[R025] Deadline: Scheduled LOI due date reached; six LOIs received in late July 2016 and considered; one (G&W) dated 07/21/2016 after the due date, with no revision of the deadline — treatment: Late bids accepted.\n\