{"type":"text","timestamp":1789825343119,"sessionID":"ses_f462b18a6ffeCc3FsyOAV29K5z","part":{"id":"prt_0b9e73c110017KzyL0kfwn02yZ_text-0","sessionID":"ses_f462b18a6ffeCc3FsyOAV29K5z","messageID":"msg_0b9e73c110017KzyL0kfwn02yZ","type":"text","text":"The workbook is complete and verified. Here's the delivery.\n\n## Deliverable\n\n**`/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/providence-worcester.xlsx`** — four visible sheets (Deal ledger, Summary, Questions, Source text) plus the hidden **Lists** sheet; 53 ledger rows, 55 source-text rows, 7 review questions. The ledger has the 14 default-visible columns and 25 labelled expandable field columns (collapsed groups O–AM), drop-down validations for all controlled columns, a filter, frozen headers/identifying columns, and 11 SUMIFS formulas in Summary that total the ledger (Include = Yes only).\n\n## What the filing shows (PWRR / G&W, DEFM14A filed 09/20/2016)\n\nProvidence & Worcester Railroad (NASDAQ: PWX) went from an unsolicited Q4 2015 expression of interest by an unnamed Class I partner (\"Party A\") to a banker-run process. GHF (later BMO) opened the process the week of 03/28/2016 by contacting 11 strategic and 18 financial buyers; 25 signed NDAs (plus late entrant Party C) with no standstill terms. Nine non-binding IOIs ($17.93–$26.50/share) arrived 05/19–06/01/2016; the two lowest were excluded and seven advanced to management presentations and a data site. After a mid-June LOI solicitation (due 07/20/2016), six LOIs arrived ($19.20–$24.00; G&W $21.15 including a $1.13 CVR, revised to $22.15), with returns marking Party B and Party D/G&W Formal and Party E's issues list Formal-borderline. On 07/27/2016 the Committee advanced G&W and Party B ($24.00); Party D ($24.00) and E ($23.81, F financing) briefly re-engaged in early August but did not continue; Party B declined to improve, and G&W's 08/12/2016 revised $25.00 all-cash LOI (CVR dropped) won the Board's superior-proposal determination. The merger agreement was signed 08/12/2016 ($25.00 cash/share; preferred as-converted 100-for-1; $3,785,000 termination fee; no financing condition; no go-shop) and announced 08/15/2016. Completion was expected in Q4 2016 — not observed in this filing.\n\n## Most consequential review items (all Pending in the workbook)\n\n- **Q1 — Round map:** one process; R1 = first outreach wave (week of 03/28/2016), R2 = mid-June LOI/mark-up solicitation, R3 = 07/27/2016 selection (Inferred final). Rejected boundaries kept as their own rows (03/14 Board decision; 03/24 authorization; 06/01 advancement; 08/04 prioritization; 08/12 final bid).\n- **Q2 — Deadlines:** 05/10 Extended, 05/19 Enforced, 07/20 Late bids accepted (G&W's LOI is dated 07/21).\n- **Q3 — Counts:** 25 wave NDAs + Party C = 26 vs the Board's \"25 … six of whom submitted\"; the two additional Class I railroads counted +2 (overlap unresolved); Party A mapped to the 16 residual non-submitters (Count 0).\n- **Q4 — Formality/conditions:** nine-IOI cohort Informal; E borderline Informal; diligence-period Heavies (G&W 3 wks, D 4 wks, C/F 30 days, E 60 days); no late-reconfirmation row (G&W restated with a new priced bid).\n- **Q5 — Outcomes:** C/D/E/F dropped 07/27 (Stated); D paused 08/02 (not an exit); D and E closed 08/04 (Inferred: residual); 16 residual non-submitters (25 − 9 = 16, Inferred); B Not selected at signing (\"Would not improve earlier offer\"); F's financing support carries no row (it had exited).\n- **Q6 — Comparability:** CVR terms; LOI expense/change-in-control caveat; labelled equity-value calculation $123,264,825 as-converted, and the ~$126.2M implied by the 3% fee.\n- **Q7 — Assigned working dates** that decide display order within rounds.\n\n## What I could not verify\n\n- **Formula recalculation and interactive features:** the SUMIFS formulas, internal source links and drop-downs were created and structurally verified (formula strings, link targets, validation ranges, and independently computed expected values), but no Excel/LibreOffice runner works in this sandbox (LibreOffice crashes even on a trivial file), so I could not click-test links/dropdowns or see cached formula results — Excel should calculate the formulas on open.\n- **Source limits:** exact NDA/notice days, identities of unnamed bidders (including which IOI prices belonged to whom), the non-submitters, and Party A's individual fate are not disclosed in the filing; those are left marked as inferred/uncertain rather than filled in.","time":{"start":1789825334296,"end":1789825343119}}}
